- 40 slots remain, ZERO are required, and no candidate meets the measured >0.115 criterion. No candidate changed the final-slot logic.\"}\n{\"id\": \"q36_gr_sigma_in_blend_oof\", \"path\": \"prompts/q36_gr_sigma_in_blend_oof.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 510, \"evidence\": \"Q19 Find A: +2.3513 nested pooled on the standalone conservative PF, interior optimum at 1.5, but tail-driven (helps 41.7%) and 3-well 5th -4.1145. The PF is only a 0.5-weight blend component and Rule #1 says averaging stabilises, so the tail failure may damp inside the blend. Slot-2 (fully-owned) improvement path.\", \"queue_reason\": \"Strongest evidence-backed candidate: Q19 measured +2.3513 nested with 1.5 a confirmed interior optimum on the standalone PF. Slot-2 (fully-owned) path.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T04:28:35Z\", \"handle\": \"55af8430\", \"prompt_hash\": \"56272138f4d42eae542e6b750319e5372c41edaa69b2b7cd25b6db6b6df341a4\", \"result\": \"DONE -- GATE FAILS on two of three. 760/760 wells usable, 0 rejected, 211.0 min. mult 1.0 -> 9.2903 (deployed base 9.2987, so the reconstruction is faithful to 0.008), 1.3 -> 9.1204 (+0.1699), 1.5 -> 9.3203 (-0.0300). NESTED picks [1.3,1.3] for +0.1699, BUT helps only 42.1% of wells with mean per-well gain -0.1197 and median -0.0569 (both NEGATIVE), and the 3-well bootstrap 5th is -1.6429 with P(>0) 0.3981. THE OPTIMUM MOVED TO EXACTLY THE PUBLIC KERNEL'S VALUE: Q19's standalone single-seed measurement put it at 1.5, but inside the ensemble and blend 1.5 is HARMFUL and 1.3 is optimal -- and 1.3 is precisely what the public 6.213 kernel uses. SUBSTANTIVE ANSWER TO THE QUESTION Q36 EXISTED TO ASK: ensembling damped MAGNITUDE (gain 2.3513 -> 0.1699, tail risk -4.1145 -> -1.6429) but NOT SIGN STRUCTURE (wells helped 41.7% -> 42.1%, essentially unchanged). Averaging cannot rescue a change that helps a minority of wells. q37 CLOSED as a result; per Q33 the next 24 h spends 0 slots.\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T08:30:00Z\", \"detail\": \"q36 full run in flight: 14 wells/4.1m \\u2192 ~3.7h ETA; smoke passed (patch effective, alignment OK)\"}\n{\"id\": \"q37_frontier_gr_sigma_public_repro\", \"path\": \"prompts/q37_frontier_gr_sigma_public_repro.md\", \"status\": \"closed\", \"priority\": 470, \"blocked_on\": \"q36_gr_sigma_in_blend_oof passing its 3-well gate\", \"evidence\": \"One-token *1.3 frontier kernel reproducing the public 6.213 operating point exactly (leonidzaporozhets/new-strategy-score-6-213). Smoke first. Held behind q21 deliberately: on current evidence it would spend a slot on a tail-driven change.\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T08:30:00Z\", \"result\": \"CLOSED -- its release condition was q36 passing the 3-well gate, and q36 FAILED two of three conditions (3-well 5th -1.6429; helps only 42.1% of wells). No frontier run, no slot.\"}\n{\"id\": \"q38_teammate_submission_provenance_recovery\", \"path\": \"prompts/q38_teammate_submission_provenance_recovery.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 570, \"queue_reason\": \"Owner asked whether we have all teammate solution data; Q30/Q35 say 54922806 provenance is still missing and actionable.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T16:24:24Z\", \"handle\": \"d8e5c924\", \"prompt_hash\": \"ef61dd1c358758b18a1d518f09e0789a865c910e2152679e6786508faa86faf5\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T16:35:00Z\", \"result\": \"DONE. Owner's question 'do we have all teammate solution data?' answered: YES. The submissions API exposes each submission's exact kernel slug AND scriptVersionId, and EVERY teammate kernel pulls successfully from this account (source + metadata incl. dataset_sources). THIS CORRECTS Q30, which recorded an 'actionable gap' telling the owner to request slug/version/datasets from the teammate -- they were available all along. Team account: 20 subs, joezzzzz 11 / leemarc223 9. HEADLINE: 54922806, our BEST public at 6.563, is the pristine Kaiwalya base PLUS `*1.3` on the PF GR-sigma line (44/45 normalised code cells identical, cell 29 inserts *1.3) -- the IDENTICAL one-token change Q19 found in the public 6.213 kernel. So the team has ALREADY banked this change on the frontier line, and closing q37 was correct for a stronger reason than recorded: it would have been a NEAR-DUPLICATE of 54922806, which the submit gate forbids. Q36's rejection is not contradicted -- Q36 measured the multiplier inside our HONEST blend, 54922806 applies it inside the FRONTIER. DISTINCTION CONFIRMED: the origin/main 6.626 repro package is 54896975 (6.669, 9 datasets, byte-identical to base), NOT the 6.563 run (54922806, 7 datasets, +*1.3) -- different kernels. CONTROLLED PAIR FOUND: 54896975 and 54923144 are normalised-identical code scoring 6.669 vs 6.678 = run-to-run spread 0.009 (their 2 extra datasets are exactly G1.3's vestigial ones). This does NOT overturn Q18: 0.009 is measurement PRECISION (same code, same 3 wells) while Q18's ~45% reversal is GENERALISATION (different models, different draw) -- both hold. It does sit awkwardly beside the recorded ~0.115 config-variance floor; flagged for reconciliation, not silently replaced. Q30's provenance caveat on 54922806 is CLOSED. Slot recommendation unchanged. ONE OPEN ITEM: kernels_pull returns the CURRENT version and it could not be confirmed it equals the submitted scriptVersionId; a short confirmation message for the teammate is drafted in report section 7.\"}\n{\"id\": \"q39_frontier_stage_localizer_no_submit\", \"path\": \"prompts/q39_frontier_stage_localizer_no_submit.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 580, \"queue_reason\": \"Revisit Q23 without public re-runs: use existing artifacts to identify any load-bearing frontier stage worth a future run.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T16:43:45Z\", \"handle\": \"ac020a1b\", \"prompt_hash\": \"d6c99a136ec09ceb4a929fdc33e8693bd76d151771f3affac50fe7961216c1fc\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T16:55:00Z\", \"result\": \"DONE, no re-run and no submission. Built the stage matrix purely from CODE DIFFS, using the teammate kernels Q38 pulled. Every family member is a single- or double-factor variant of one pristine base: 54896975 and 54923144 diff to NONE (code-identical replicate pair, 6.669 vs 6.678 -> same-code spread 0.009, baseline mean 6.6735); 54922806 = base + '*1.3' on GR sigma (cell 29); 54968060 = base + overlap override False (cell 0); 54990075 = overlap OFF + SP45-only truncation; 55064411 = overlap OFF + _BH_CAP 2->0 (cell 42); the public 6.213 kernel = the IDENTICAL '*1.3' change as 54922806. HEADLINE CORRECTION: the simulator's 'retrieval penalty = 0.080 (= 54968060 6.643 vs 54922806 6.563)' is a CONFOUND, because those kernels differ in TWO stages. Decomposed against the pristine baseline: overlap/retrieval = -0.031 (turning overlap OFF slightly HELPS) and GR sigma = -0.1105, and -0.1105-(-0.031) = -0.080 reproduces the recorded number as a difference of two different stages. So retrieval is NOT worth 0.080; 54922806's edge is the GR-sigma multiplier, which is not a train-duplicate lookup and does NOT go inert on novel wells -- meaning 54922806 does not converge onto 54968060 under H-hidden, which is what produced Q18's tie structure and its '+0.000 worst' price for our-account-first. COUNTERWEIGHT KEPT EXPLICIT: Q36 measured that same multiplier on 760 wells with truth and it helps only 42.1% of wells with a negative median, so the stage carrying the public edge is the one our held-out evidence says does not transfer. STAGE MATRIX: prefix calibration and model-package fallback are MEASURED INERT (alpha=0.0; guard-rejected); overlap is NOT load-bearing (~0.03, uncertain sign); bimodal hedge helps public +0.052 but Q14 shows local harm; post-SP45 stages help +0.047 JOINTLY; learned-trajectory blend is the only genuinely UNKNOWN stage, bounded at <=0.047. NO stage change clears the information-value threshold, so no submission is proposed. Queued q53_simulator_retrieval_penalty_correction -- zero cost, arithmetic only.\"}\n{\"id\": \"q40_transition_model_search\", \"path\": \"prompts/q40_transition_model_search.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 590, \"queue_reason\": \"Q17 closed emission/AUC; transition model is the remaining untested alignment lever.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T17:13:49Z\", \"handle\": \"92ea024a\", \"prompt_hash\": \"d72a99bcf74a07b3665d5aa337d37e495f1c7583ef6973abf8e975a33ab70ff4\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T17:25:00Z\", \"result\": \"GATE FAILS ALL THREE CONDITIONS. No Kaggle path, no submission, quota 0/5. The entire transition model is one term (lam*|t-s|/BAND, one parameter, previous-state only). Six families tested, all strictly containing it -- l1, l2, huber, drift (heel-estimated trajectory prior), curv, l1curv -- 45 arms, 40 eval wells, splits by well, every parameter nested, validated on DP OUTPUT ONLY per Q17's rule. RESULT: NO VARIANT BEATS THE BASELINE. l1 lam=60 = 12.170 is the best of all 45 arms and exactly reproduces Q10. Best non-l1 is huber(150,5)=12.313. All 45 nested together: 14.452 vs 12.601 = -1.851, helps only 20.0% of wells, 3-well 5th -5.845. INFORMATIVE NEGATIVE: drift failed hardest (-11.475) despite mu~0 in most wells, so the mechanism was measured -- degeneracy control gives max|drift-l1| = 0.000000 on the 11 wells with mu EXACTLY 0 (so no implementation error), mean degradation +2.216 on the 29 with mu!=0, corr(|mu|, degradation) = +0.796, DP steps median 477, accumulated pull |mu|xsteps median 48.4 ft vs a 12 ft RMSE scale. THE DP INTEGRATES THE TRANSITION TERM: a per-step directional prior compounds by path length, so a median-unbiased drift estimate is NOT neutral. SAME FAILURE CLASS AS Q13 (directional pull, fine per row, cumulatively harmful). PROPOSED RULE: judge any per-step directional DP term against the ACCUMULATED pull (|estimate| x steps), not the per-step magnitude. CLOSES the transition lever within the penalty-shape and local-prior family; with Q17 both named levers on the alignment line are now measured. NOT closed: learned or state-dependent transitions, per-well adaptive lambda, and beam width K/BAND.\"}\n{\"id\": \"q41_nonhomogeneous_ensemble_search\", \"path\": \"prompts/q41_nonhomogeneous_ensemble_search.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 600, \"queue_reason\": \"Search only non-homogeneous ensembles that can change final-slot logic or clear the >0.115 information threshold.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T17:28:51Z\", \"handle\": \"eecb5163\", \"prompt_hash\": \"1214cdb0f10c819c1495965c5ffb81fc4eac68e6eed92d5f2b6e75926bd8e90b\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T17:40:00Z\", \"result\": \"CLOSED with an exact reason. No submission, quota 0/5. BLOCKER on the task's first arm: honest+frontier CANNOT be validated by well -- the frontier exists locally only as TEST-SET submission CSVs (14,151 rows, 3 wells, NO truth), so no honest+frontier mix can be scored, bootstrapped or gated; producing it needs a fresh frontier GPU run that Q33's budget rules out. Recorded as a blocker, not guessed at. On the honest family (760 wells with truth) 355 arms were built -- all member pairs at 9 weights, equal-weight triples, per-row median over 3 and 5, and a 5-member mean. Error-correlation with deployed identifies the genuinely decorrelated axis: dwt 0.868 / pf 0.831 vs structural variants at 0.96-0.97. NESTED across all 355: gain +0.3346, helps 58.8% of wells -- TWO of three gate conditions PASS, the best any candidate has done -- but 3-well bootstrap 5th is -1.3687, so the gate FAILS. THE VARIANCE HYPOTHESIS IS REFUTED: 0 of 355 arms have a 3-well 5th > 0, and the arms with the LEAST negative 5th are those changing the deployed line LEAST, monotonically in BOTH directions -- the 3-well 5th is maximised by changing nothing. Arithmetic: with per-well gain mean ~0.35 and std ~1.3, the n=3 5th percentile is ~-0.88, so clearing zero needs mean gain >~1.2, over 3x the best available. AND the apparent gain is MEMBER SUBSTITUTION not ensembling: the best ensemble 8.4984 beats the best single member topk96_l75 8.5070 by only +0.0086. RECORDED NOT RECOMMENDED: topk96_l75 is 0.3556 better than deployed on OOF and has never been submitted, but fails the 3-well gate, correlates 0.9445 with deployed (little slot-2 diversity), and N4 puts OOF->public transfer at 1.659x.\"}\n{\"id\": \"q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy\", \"path\": \"prompts/q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 610, \"queue_reason\": \"Slot-2 honest line remains useful; test whether its errors have group-level actionable structure beyond Q16 row-level sign failure.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T17:43:52Z\", \"handle\": \"199bbf61\", \"prompt_hash\": \"64c6aeb73a969792fa46d6cc96a2f4e947e5330f8e6dbd0cd0f662a7cf7c5906\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T17:55:00Z\", \"result\": \"LINE CLOSED, no group-level intervention proposed. No submission, quota 0/5. TAXONOMY built over 13 test-available segments on 760 wells / 3.72M rows: quintile spreads of the mean signed residual run 0.5-1.7 ft and LOOK like structure. SPLIT-HALF TEST on two disjoint 380-well halves shows only 2 of 8 reproduce -- dwt_pf_disagree (+0.815) and struct_contrib (+0.802), exactly the two ROW-level features -- while EVERY well-level feature ANTI-correlates (nnb -0.566, mean_incl -0.648, closest_all -0.751, prefix_frac -0.270, well_md -0.290, tortuosity -0.162), i.e. their patterns flip sign, which is what noise does. THE ARITHMETIC: per-well mean residual std is 6.673 across wells and a quintile holds ~152 wells, so a group mean's standard error is ~0.54 -- the same size as the observed spreads. Rows within a well are correlated, so the effective n is 152 WELLS, not 744,000 rows. PROPOSED RULE: when segmenting by a well-level feature, compare the spread against sigma_well/sqrt(n_wells) before calling it structure. OOF GROUP-CONSTANT CORRECTIONS: best is struct_contrib at +0.0065 (0.07% of an 8.86 RMSE), 2 of 13 positive, 0 of 13 clear the 3-well 5th, and NO segment helps a majority of wells (max 49.1%). Even the two reproducible 