ensemble in both slots costs +0.958 ft. Consistent with Q44's independently measured 0.456 diverse-pair value because it is the same quantity. Harmful BEFORE the third-artifact slot cost is counted. THE CHEAPEST CLOSURE is q24 (frontier run-variance control): its objective was achieved externally FOR FREE by Q45's find (5 kernels resubmitted 14 times unchanged, sd 0.027-0.037), a larger and cleaner measurement than several GPU runs plus quota would have bought. ALSO CLOSED: q23 (Q39 did the stage localisation with NO run from code diffs, and Q45 re-priced the residual stages BELOW the measured 0.03 readability floor -- hedge +0.052 at ~1.7 sd, post-SP45 +0.047 at ~1.6 sd); q32 (merged into q22, which is done); q34 (duplicate of q20, which is done); and q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup, which sat on 'hold' with NO RECORDED REASON while carrying can_submit=true max_submit_cost=1 -- a submission-capable row with no rationale, exactly the risk this review removes -- and is closed on substance too since it proposes an EMISSION improvement that Q17 measured as decoupled from DP quality and Q57 showed is the wrong kind (directional content, not AUC). CONFIRMED DEFERRED, each re-verified rather than assumed: q26 STRENGTHENED (Q45's refresh found 1136 kernels, +42%, still nothing below 6.2, and parsed advertised scores are triage-only); q27 stays deferred with a narrower successor RECORDED BUT NOT QUEUED (Q57 sharpened the constraint to DIRECTIONAL content, so the well-posed question is whether any test-available signal predicts the SIGN of the next TVT move out-of-fold -- not queued because the alignment line cannot become submittable before 2026-08-05 so its expected value for the outcome is ~0); q29 date trigger still unmet (needs >= 2026-08-03), with two notes added -- the idle-queue risk it warned about is gone since five rows are queued, but that also means nothing re-activates IT automatically so state.json's endgame_action_required remains the only mechanism, AN