-31\"}\n{\"id\": \"q50_ownership_first_candidate_search\", \"path\": \"prompts/q50_ownership_first_candidate_search.md\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"priority\": 690, \"queue_reason\": \"Find whether an our-account candidate can replace teammate 54922806 without meaningful score loss or with provenance gain.\", \"blocked_handle\": \"98ed15c4\", \"blocked_at\": \"2026-07-30T01:14:20Z\", \"blocked_detail\": \"Login expired\", \"requeued_after\": \"claude_login_expired_codex_takeover_2026-07-31\"}\n{\"id\": \"q51_owner_message_pack\", \"path\": \"prompts/q51_owner_message_pack.md\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"priority\": 700, \"queue_reason\": \"Prepare teammate request and final-selection coordination messages based on Q38/Q46.\", \"blocked_handle\": \"3d355393\", \"blocked_at\": \"2026-07-30T01:29:22Z\", \"blocked_detail\": \"Login expired\", \"requeued_after\": \"claude_login_expired_codex_takeover_2026-07-31\"}\n{\"id\": \"q52_next_queue_builder_after_q38_q51\", \"path\": \"prompts/q52_next_queue_builder_after_q38_q51.md\", \"status\": \"queued\", \"priority\": 710, \"queue_reason\": \"Avoid another idle queue; add only evidence-driven executable tasks or explicitly declare no high-value work remains.\", \"blocked_handle\": \"6f5484a3\", \"blocked_at\": \"2026-07-30T01:44:24Z\", \"blocked_detail\": \"Login expired\", \"requeued_after\": \"claude_login_expired_codex_takeover_2026-07-31\"}\n{\"id\": \"q53_simulator_retrieval_penalty_correction\", \"path\": \"prompts/q53_simulator_retrieval_penalty_correction.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 305, \"evidence\": \"Q39 decomposition: the simulator encodes retrieval=0.080 from a two-stage confound; measured against the pristine baseline overlap is -0.031 and GR sigma is -0.1105. Zero cost, arithmetic over recorded scores.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T16:58:47Z\", \"handle\": \"36105aa2\", \"prompt_hash\": \"687fbf9d90763b870be38490ad1f5a627e5a7933e943bd1cbce26067a5342171\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T17:10:00Z\", \"result\": \"DONE (arithmetic only; no GPU, no smoke, no submission, quota 0/5). HEADLINE: Q18's conclusion SURVIVES the Q39 correction but its REASONING did not. Two axes were needed because correcting retrieval alone would have flipped the answer: retrieval_delta in {-0.031 measured, 0.0, +0.080 old} x sigma_transfers in {True, False} (whether 54922806's GR-sigma edge survives on novel wells -- NOT a strawman, since Q36 measured that exact multiplier on 760 wells with truth and it helps only 42.1% of wells with a negative median, so False is the evidence-supported arm). RESULT: under the measured + supported cell (-0.031, False) the price of our-account-first is +0.0005 worst / +0.0402 mean -- essentially Q18's +0.000/+0.040. TWO WRONG INPUTS WERE CANCELLING: the old model overstated retrieval (+0.080 vs -0.031) AND implicitly let the GR-sigma edge survive under H-hidden; correcting both moves the price 0.0005, correcting only one would have moved it to +0.080 and flipped the conclusion. (1) RECOMMENDED PAIR unchanged in any way that survives noise -- score-first nominally shifts to 54896975+54922806 by 0.0045, HALF the 0.009 replicate spread, with family diversity 0; diversity- and provenance-first stay at 54922806+54844628. (2) TIE STRUCTURE still heavily tied: 6-11 pairs vs Q18's 9, and 11 in the supported cell. (3) PRICE not materially changed. THE WHOLE SLOT-1 QUESTION REDUCES TO ONE UNRESOLVED QUANTITY: does GR-sigma widening help on NOVEL wells? The H-hidden gap is 0.0005 if it does not transfer and 0.1110 if it does. DECISION: no change -- it remains an OWNERSHIP JUDGEMENT, and no additional public evidence can settle it, so no submission would help (consistent with Q33's 0-slot conclusion). The old simulator scripts were left UNMODIFIED so the Q18 record stays reproducible; scripts/q53_simulator_retrieval_correction.py supersedes them.\"}\n{\"id\": \"q54_dp_hard_path_constraints\", \"path\": \"prompts/q54_dp_hard_path_constraints.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 625, \"evidence\": \"Q43 P1: the DP has NO global constraint and NO slope limits; hard admissibility masks bound accumulated deviation REGARDLESS of path length, the structural complement of the soft per-step family Q40 closed. ~10 min on the existing harness.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T19:13:56Z\", \"handle\": \"e0d6746b\", \"prompt_hash\": \"9fce255be865a85ab069d076c0bd77a53ece037cf005c873a7de5bc1ddd20526\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T19:25:00Z\", \"result\": \"GATE FAILS all three. No submission, quota 0/5. SCOPE CORRECTION made before running: the Itakura slope-limit half is ALREADY CLOSED by N1, with a better geometry-derived per-step interval, so only the genuinely untested CUMULATIVE corridor |state_j - anchor| <= C was run. CONTROLS: C=inf reproduces run_dp to 0.0000000000 at all four lambdas; binding diagnostic C=2 21.9% / C=3 14.7% / C=5 5.3% / C=10 1.4% / C=20 0.4% / C=inf 0.0% -- the FIRST smoke repeated N1's trap exactly (C=40 bound 0.0%), and the cause was measured rather than reported as 'no effect'. THE HEADLINE: at the optimal lam=60 the DP path deviates from the anchor by a median max of 3.0 ft while the TRUTH deviates 19.4 ft -- the DP is OVER-DAMPED, not under-constrained, so a corridor can only restrict it further and any corridor tight enough to bind would EXCLUDE THE TRUTH. This explains Q10's headline: the DP beats the flat anchor 12.170 vs 12.722 because its path IS nearly the flat anchor. RESULT: corridor and penalty are SUBSTITUTES not complements -- at lam=5 the corridor rescues +3.12 (16.009 -> 12.887, the level lambda alone reaches), but the best with corridor+lambda is 12.138 vs 12.170 with lambda alone. That directly answers Q43's premise: the hard cap does NOT do something the soft penalty structurally cannot, because the binding issue is not accumulation. NESTED +0.031, helps only 2.5% of wells (the lowest win rate in the project, consistent since C=10 binds just 1.4% of steps), 3-well 5th -0.518. CLOSES hard global path constraints; with N1 and Q40 the transition model is now closed across soft penalties, per-step hard bounds AND global corridors. PREDICTION RECORDED for q55: with paths already within +-3 ft, averaging near-optimal paths should move very little -- q55 must measure the beam spread FIRST. q56 unaffected (targets the PF).\"}\n{\"id\": \"q55_dp_decoder_averaging\", \"path\": \"prompts/q55_dp_decoder_averaging.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 626, \"evidence\": \"Q43 P2: beam-average and soft-min Bellman, both untested on the DP. Precedent: Q21 found the deployed PF ensemble is already a softmax at T=5 sitting at a nested optimum. ~10 min. | Q54 PREDICTION: DP paths sit within +-3 ft of the anchor while truth moves +-19.4, so averaging near-optimal paths may move very little. MEASURE THE K=6 BEAM SPREAD FIRST and report it before anything else.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T19:28:58Z\", \"handle\": \"1d3cafbd\", \"prompt_hash\": \"8d173ae2dac2f9895f78fd90cce3bf4a94188a1c1f580a4366100bcbe4d1dd7f\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T20:03:00Z\", \"result\": \"GATE FAILS all three arms (beam-average, soft-min, both). No submission, quota 0/5. The run COMPLETED despite the API-500 that marked this row blocked; log and report are on disk. BEAM SPREAD MEASURED FIRST as Q54 required: the six beams agree to ~0.1 grid units on average and the best-vs-worst beam differs by only 0.19-0.24 RMSE, so beam averaging is INERT BY CONSTRUCTION -- Q54's prediction confirmed. Degeneracy control: beam-avg at T->0 recovers run_dp (4e-5 at lam=60). HEADLINE, and the most consequential structural finding of the alignment line: an EXACT VITERBI over all states achieves a strictly LOWER objective cost than the beam on 38/40, 31/40 and 25/40 wells at lam=20/60/150, yet a WORSE RMSE at every lambda (32.609 vs 13.169; 15.390 vs 12.170; 12.628 vs 12.478). The DP objective (emission + lam*|dstate|) is MISALIGNED with RMSE, so solving it better makes predictions worse and the beam's greedy suboptimality is PROTECTIVE rather than a defect. This is also the mechanism behind Q54's over-damping: the beam is damped because it is greedy, and a constraint cannot add what greediness already supplies. Note the exact-vs-beam RMSE gap shrinks monotonically with lambda (19.4 -> 3.2 -> 0.15), i.e. large lambda flattens the objective until its true optimum coincides with what greedy search was doing anyway -- so Q10's lam=60, Q40's 45 arms and Q54's corridors were all tuning an objective whose exact optimum is worse than the approximate solver's answer. NESTED: beam +0.035 helps 52.5% 3-well 5th -0.007; soft-min +0.230 helps 32.5% 5th -1.420; both +0.231 helps 65.0% (the highest per-well win rate the alignment line has produced) 5th -1.419. Best single pooled number ever on this line: fb lam=150 g=0.2 -> 11.352, but nested it delivers only +0.230 because the folds pick different arms. CLOSES the decoder side; with Q17 (emission) and Q40/N1/Q54 (transition) the alignment line is closed on all three sides, and the remaining lever is REDEFINING THE OBJECTIVE, not tuning it.\"}\n{\"id\": \"q57_dip_state_augmented_dp\", \"path\": \"prompts/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 628, \"queue_reason\": \"Q45 architecture scan: tiktoktrendz/rogii-dip-aware-hmm-gbm searches 41 dip rates with momentum, i.e. state = (TVT, dip). Every transition arm Q40/N1/Q54 closed and every decoder Q55 tested used a TVT-ONLY state, so state augmentation changes the objective's shape rather than its coefficients -- the one direction Q55's closure left open. Reuses the Q10/Q40/Q54 harness with mandatory degeneracy and activation controls.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T21:32:00Z\", \"handle\": \"00b8b89e\", \"prompt_hash\": \"f019eda21543f39b380fbb7fd31f7635a98b84f8a5db5bbcab4c3490d9e8966f\", \"result\": \"GATE FAILS all three conditions. No submission, quota 0/5. HARNESS VALIDATED FIRST: the ndip=1 nu=0 mu=60 arm reproduces Q10's recorded l1 lam=60 baseline EXACTLY at 12.170, and the degeneracy control is exact (max|dip_dp - run_dp| = 0.0000000000). MODEL: state (s,d), cost C[j,s'] + mu*|s'-(s+d')|/BAND + nu*|d'-d|, which strictly CONTAINS the deployed DP. THE FIRST SMOKE WAS EXACTLY INERT and the cause was priced, not guessed: a dip's penalty is immediate while its payoff is DEFERRED (switch on costs nu once, saves mu*|d|/BAND on every later step, ~477 per well), so a globally greedy top-K beam prunes every d!=0 candidate first -- the arm was UNREACHABLE, not failing. Fixed with per-dip beams, which also hand the augmented model 30 beams against the baseline's 6, i.e. MORE search, making the comparison conservative against the conclusion. This is Q55 from the other side: there the beam's greedy suboptimality was PROTECTIVE, here the same greediness BLOCKS a different model from being explored. RESULT on 40 wells: EVERY augmented arm has strictly LOWER objective cost and strictly WORSE RMSE. Dose-response, monotone in both directions at nu=0: cost -569.7 -> -624.4 -> -633.6 while RMSE 12.170 -> 14.850 -> 19.929 for ndip 1 -> 3 -> 5. At ndip=5 the DP is WORSE THAN THE FLAT ANCHOR (12.722), i.e. beaten by predicting no change at all. THE HEADLINE, WHICH CORRECTS THE SMOKE-BASED DRAFT: the 8-well smoke's well kept the dip nearly off (5.9% of steps, path deviation unchanged at 3.1 ft) and the draft concluded 'the DP declines the freedom it is given' -- ON 40 WELLS THAT IS WRONG. The dip is active on 42-46% of steps, changes on up to 54%, and the path deviation rises from 4.9 ft to 16.1-21.1 ft against 36.0 ft of truth, with Q40 accumulated pull 15-18 grid units. SO THE AUGMENTATION DOES CURE Q54'S OVER-DAMPING -- the mobility lands in the right ballpark -- AND THE RMSE GETS 2.7 TO 7.8 FT WORSE. The real finding: the DP can be made to move the right amount, and moving the right amount in the WRONG DIRECTION is worse than not moving. The damping was never a limitation of the transition model; it was PROTECTION against an emission that cannot say which way to go, so extra mobility amplifies emission error rather than adding information. Secondary consistent pattern: the useful nu grows with dip width (ndip=3 best at nu=0, ndip=5 best at nu=1) -- more freedom needs more damping, and the best augmented arm is always the one closest to switched off. NESTED: picks the un-augmented baseline in BOTH folds, so selected 12.170 vs baseline 12.170, gain +0.000, helps 0.0%, 3-well 5th +0.000 -- the zeros are not a degenerate run but the cleanest possible negative, the augmentation is never chosen on held-out wells at any width or penalty. COST CONTROL: the ndip=9 arm was dropped mid-round and ndip=3 substituted (~0.36x the cost) because ndip=9 projected 60+ min on a 2-core box shared with q56's 760-well run; stopped by verified PID, recorded in the report rather than made silently. CLOSES the state-space side, so the alignment DP is now closed on FOUR sides: emission (Q17), transition (Q40/N1/Q54), decoder (Q55), state space (Q57). AND IT LOCATES THE BINDING CONSTRAINT: since the augmented path demonstrably CAN travel the distance truth travels, the failure is not reach, expressiveness or tuning -- it is that the emission lacks directional content. No further transition, decoder or state-space device can help; three have now each made things worse the same way, and Q17 already measured that a large AUC gain does not supply that content.\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T22:55:00Z\"}\n{\"id\": \"q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing\", \"path\": \"prompts/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 629, \"queue_reason\": \"Q56 measured the ancestral-path PF smoother at +0.2541 nested on 760 wells inside the deployed blend, helping 68.9% of wells with a POSITIVE median and a verified mechanism (monotone lookahead dose, savgol control ~10%). It fails only the 3-well bootstrap 5th (-0.3238, P(>0) 0.7919). The blend-level number is not the deployed line's number: the gated structural-field stage worth +0.436 was FITTED AGAINST THE FORWARD PF and must be re-fitted against the smoothed one. Q44 measured the honest line as the largest positive term in the final-pair decision (~0.46 ft mean as the decorrelated best-of-2 member), so improving it improves the slot the project relies on.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T23:32:00Z\", \"handle\": \"cb20d18c\", \"prompt_hash\": \"c9c64eb97915d098e3e75d05f4d2582eb4b3fa261e6fbe7b9cfd95a1733969f8\", \"result\": \"IN PROGRESS: the deployed line is now EXACTLY reproduced from saved arrays, and the NS=64 row-level PF run is in flight (ETA ~02:50 UTC, log reports/logs/q58_pf_produce_2026-07-30.log). No submission yet, quota 0/5. PREMISE CORRECTED BY READING THE CODE: the task assumed the structural-field stage 'was fitted against the forward PF'. It does not depend on the PF at all -- struct is an IDW field over same-group train wells plus the target's own heel anchor, already computed for all 3,721,471 rows in struct_oof.npz. The ONLY things fitted against the forward PF are W and the gate threshold, so the re-fit is arithmetic over saved arrays with no PF re-run. That let the round split into a slow producer (row-level PF predictions, the artifact Q56 failed to save) and a fast evaluator that can be iterated. REPRODUCTION CONTROL, and it found a real trap: using the aligned frame's per-row nnb/closest_surv columns the line does NOT reproduce -- 2139 rows wrong (0.057%), max diff 4.59 ft, RMSE 8.8634 vs 8.8626, with the residual concentrated in 6 wells of 760 and 1731 rows in 8b95d6d1 alone (closest_surv 1011.1, just outside a <1000 gate, yet the deployed line gated it IN). The deployed gate is built from struct_oof.npz's OWN per-well meta (meta_nnb, meta_closest). With that: rebuilt RMSE 8.8626 exactly, only 9 rows of 3.72M differ by >0.01 at max 0.0182 (float32 rounding), gated 87.3% vs the ledger's 87%. The weight was RECOVERED FROM THE DEPLOYED COLUMN rather than taken from the ledger: implied W median 0.1500 (p5 0.1497, p95 0.1503) on gated rows and 0.0000 off-gate. So the stage is fully characterised by (meta gate, W=0.15) and substituting a smoothed PF is a clean one-factor change. RECORDED AS A LATENT TRAP FOR FUTURE ROUNDS: the aligned frame's nnb/closest_surv columns are NOT the deployed gate and silently disagree on 6 wells. PRODUCER: NS=64, the DEPLOYED config, which removes the caveat Q36 and Q56 both had to carry AND buys a free control -- the stored pf column in aligned_preds.npz IS the deployed NS=64 forward PF, so pf_fwd can be checked directly against it. Smoother and trellis twin imported unchanged from q56; the producer re-runs the byte-for-byte degeneracy assertion itself. Smoke passed (6 wells, NS=4, 6/6 usable, 27,945 rows). SUBMISSION POSITION PRE-REGISTERED before the number is known: justified only if the end-to-end line beats 8.8626 by a margin surviving nesting AND the output is materially different from 54844628; the negative 3-well 5th at blend level constrains what a PUBLIC score can resolve (Q41, Q44's 2.40 ft draw sd), not novel-well quality; and Q44 measured slot 2 as the largest positive term in the final-pair decision (~0.46 ft mean / ~0.94 ft tail as the decorrelated best-of-2 member), which is the strongest argument for spending one of five idle slots.\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T23:44:09Z\", \"detail\": \"q58 smoothed PF: reproduced 8.8626 RMSE, meta thresholds locked, producer ready for struct refit\"}\n{\"id\": \"q56_pf_backward_smoothing\", \"path\": \"prompts/q56_pf_backward_smoothing.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 627, \"evidence\": \"Q43 P3: the PF is forward-only although the entire toe GR is observable at prediction time -- a real modelling gap. FFBSi is an averaging operation, so Q40 compounding does not apply. Hours; smoke first; score inside the blend. | Q45 REFERENCE: yangrangrong/rogii-notebook4383-v8 is an independent PUBLIC implementation of this exact lever (sequential PF, apply_rts_smoother backward RTS pass over the retained trellis, apply_fixed_lag_smoother, N_PARTICLES=200 N_SEEDS=64, 9 cells, 0% overlap with the Kaiwalya family). Useful for mechanics -- which quantities to retain and where the backward pass attaches. But it advertises NO score and was last run 2026-06-12, which is weak evidence AGAINST rather than for. Pulled to reports/logs/q45_pulled/yangrangrong__rogii-notebook4383-v8/.\", \"prompt_hash\": \"6d8d816f8a91ddbe52046908afacb72ffb2c9c3ba6121fc8f5c475fc98007387\", \"detail\": \"Q56 smoke pass: backward smoothing +0.513, nested +0.6050, 3-well 5th +0.0836\", \"requeued_note\": \"Reset from blocked to queued by Q45. The block detail was a transient API error (API Error: 529 Overloaded. This is a server-side issue, usua), not an evidence-based outcome, and no work was executed on the turn. q55 carried the same blocked mark yet its run had COMPLETED and its report was on disk, so leaving infrastructure blocks in place silently drops real work.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T21:16:00Z\", \"handle\": \"c34cb597\", \"result\": \"GATE FAILS on the 3-well condition; the other two PASS. No submission (can_submit=false), quota 0/5. 760/760 wells usable, 0 rejected, 108.6 min. RECONSTRUCTION CHECK: the forward arm gives 9.2903 against the deployed blend base 9.2987 -- the same 0.008 NS=32-vs-64 offset Q36 measured, so the pipeline is faithful. RESULT: full smoother alpha=1.0 -> 9.0362, NESTED +0.2541, helps 68.9% of held-out wells, mean per-well +0.3686, MEDIAN +0.2044; 3-well bootstrap 5th -0.3238, 50th +0.3071, 95th +1.2561, P(>0) 0.7919. THE SMOKE OVER-STATED THE SIZE BY 58% (+0.6050 -> +0.2541, helps 91.7% -> 68.9%, 3-well 5th +0.0836 -> -0.3238) and the report predicted that direction in advance because the smoke wells were easier (forward 7.88 vs 9.29). A 12-WELL SMOKE IS AN ACTIVATION CHECK, NOT A SIZE -- that is the reusable lesson. EVERYTHING THAT MADE THE SMOKE CREDIBLE SURVIVED AT FULL SCALE: lookahead dose-response still monotone on 760 wells (block25 +0.0205, block100 +0.0768, block400 +0.1898, full +0.3686), monotone in alpha for every mode, and the Savitzky-Golay denoising control buys only +0.0383 against the smoother's +0.3686, so ~90% of the gain is lookahead information a symmetric filter cannot supply (the smoke put it at 92%). NOT TAIL-DRIVEN: 68.9% helped with a POSITIVE median, the exact opposite of the GR-sigma multiplier's signature (Q19/Q36: 41.7%/42.1% helped, NEGATIVE median) which the ledger records before the 54878409 public regression. ON THE FAILING CONDITION: P(gain>0) is 0.7919, Q41 showed the 3-well 5th is maximised by changing nothing, and Q44 measured the 3-well draw's difference-sd at 2.40 ft, ~9x this effect -- so that condition mostly constrains what a PUBLIC score can resolve, not novel-well quality. This does NOT convert the FAIL into a PASS and is not used to. FOR SCALE: the deployed structural-field stage is worth +0.436 (9.2987 -> 8.8626) and this smoother is worth +0.2625 against the same starting point -- about 60% of that whole stage, from a change that adds no new inputs. DISPOSITION: not promoted on this evidence; queued q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing to reproduce the smoother inside the honest kernel and RE-FIT the structural-field stage against the smoothed PF (it was fitted against the FORWARD PF, so its +0.436 is not transferable as-is), then apply the submit gate. The blend-level number is not the deployed line's number.\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T23:20:00Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
