ent_smoke_2026-07-28.md-62-\nreports/g32_learned_alignment_smoke_2026-07-28.md-63-```\n--\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-27-\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-28-Per well: cut the known prefix at `CUT`; re-run the PF forward with only `K_cal` known; measure the error\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-29-on the held-out prefix slice (the signal available at inference) and the error on the toe (the target).\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-30-\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-31-**A confound had to be separated first.** If the signal and the target are both taken from the *same\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:32:truncated run*, they share the degradation caused by having a shorter prefix, which inflates the\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:33:correlation. The deployment-honest pairing is: signal from the **truncated** run (that is what inference\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-34-can compute), target from the **full-prefix** run (that is the error a correction must fix).\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-35-\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-36-## Result (30 train wells, PF forward, both cut fractions)\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-37-\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-38-```\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-39-CUT = 0.70   held-out median 493 rows | toe median 5182 rows\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:40:  [confounded]  corr(bias_hold, bias_toe from the SAME truncated run) = +0.6589  -> 43.4%\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-41-  [deployment]  corr(bias_hold, bias_toe from the FULL-prefix run)    = +0.1862  ->  3.5%\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-42-  corr(drift_hold, drift_toe) = +0.1431 -> 2.0%\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-43-  best scalar a=0.408: toe-bias std 7.632 -> 7.500; variance removed 3.4% (IN-SAMPLE upper bound)\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-44-\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-45-CUT = 0.50\n--\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-73-\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-74-`54844628` is unchanged and remains the slot-2 recommendation under all three criteria.\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-75-\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-76-### Transferable finding (worth carrying into any future calibration work)\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-77-\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:78:**Never measure a calibration signal and its target on the same truncated run.** Doing so inflated the\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-79-apparent correlation by 3–4× here (0.659 vs 0.186; 0.376 vs 0.074). Any prefix-calibration design — ours\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:80:or the frontier's — must pair a truncated-run signal with a full-prefix target, or it will report a\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-81-signal that does not exist at inference. This is consistent with what the frontier's own calibration does\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-82-in practice: G1.2 found its selected `balanced` profile applied `alpha = 0.0` (no movement at all), and\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-83-`54990075` showed the post-SP45 stages as a whole are only mildly useful on public.\n--\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-91-## 5. What this changes\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-92-\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-93-1. **`54968060` is validated as a genuine no-retrieval frontier run** — the slot-2 candidacy rests on\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-94-   solid ground