 hedge, not merely a diagnostic.\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-33-\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-34-**Caveat (decisive):** this is measured against train-copy TVT, and 2026-07-22 established that local\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-35-truth-space accuracy does not predict the leaderboard at the ≲0.1 scale (our own 54878409 was better\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-36-locally, worse on public). So \"frontier better locally\" is suggestive, not conclusive. The pending public\n--\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-2-\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-3-Round 2 of the rotation pipeline. **Submitted: ref `54990075` (PENDING).** Today 1/5 used, 4 remaining.\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-4-\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-5-## What it is\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-6-\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md:7:The frontier notebook truncated after its **SP45 projection** stage: a final cell writes\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-8-`sp45_projection_submission.csv` as `submission.csv`, with row-count and finiteness asserts so the patch\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-9-cannot silently no-op. Built on the overlap-OFF notebook, so **retrieval/overlap stays OFF** — this is a\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-10-no-lookup candidate by construction.\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-11-\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-12-It removes the frontier's post-SP45 stages: learned-trajectory blend (w=0.60), visible-prefix\n--\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-14-\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-15-## The one question that dominates variant value: H-visible vs H-hidden\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-16-\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-17-- **H-visible** (public/private = row splits of the 3 visible wells): overlap + prefix-calibration are\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-18-  legitimate and the frontier family's public advantage carries to private.\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md:19:- **H-hidden** (rerun scores novel wells): overlap goes inert (no train duplicate), prefix-calibration\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-20-  still applies (any well has a known heel), and the family reverts toward its base PF/beam quality.\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-21-\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-22-The variant queue is designed to *probe* this without needing organizer confirmation.\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-23-\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-24-## Queue — each: smoke (FAST) → full → judge\n--\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-29-As the transition penalty rises, the DP **converges toward the flat-anchor baseline from above and never\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-30-crosses it**. At `LAM=60` the path search is still slightly worse than simply holding the anchor TVT\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-31-constant (13.638 vs 13.278), and the whole family sits far above the honest pipeline's ~8.86 ft.\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-32-\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-33-The reading is unambiguous: **every amount of GR-emission influence makes the prediction worse than\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md:34:ignoring GR entirely.** The optimum of this formulation is the degenerate one.\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-35-\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-36-The beam adds nothing either: top-1 → oracle top-8 improves by 0.035 / 0.107 / 0.559 ft across the three\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-37-settings. The K paths are near-duplicates, so a ranker over them (the earlier top-K line) would have\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-38-nothing to choose between — consistent with that li