ally the same thing. **The entire 6.5→7.9\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-55-public gap is the overlap lookup on the visible wells.** This makes the two-slot hedge exact:\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-56-\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-57-- **H-visible**: the overlap-ON 6.5 family wins (overlap returns near-truth). Slot `54922806` (6.563).\n--\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-66-**+0.9194**. It is a re-weighting of the same field, not a decorrelated second source. The two-field\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-67-combination being *worse* than either alone (−0.2298) confirms the redundancy — there is nothing\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-68-independent for a second coefficient to buy.\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-69-\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-70-Caveat on absolute values: this subset is **ungated** and easy (base 7.39 vs the global 9.30), so the\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md:71:structural field is net-negative here where the deployed gated version is positive. Only the *relative*\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-72-comparison and the correlation are informative.\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-73-\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-74-## Disposition\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-75-\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-76-- The GR-weighted variant is not a decorrelated third source. It could be re-examined later as a minor\n--\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-55-\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-56-## Disposition\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-57-\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-58-A3/A4/A5 are **informational, HOLD**. They confirm the 6.