le negative — the augmentation is never chosen on held-out wells at any width or penalty.\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-181-\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-182-## 6. What this closes\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-183-\n--\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-186-| side | round | verdict |\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-187-|---|---|---|\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-188-| emission | Q17 | AUC is decoupled from DP quality (+0.056 AUC bought 0.167 RMSE) |\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-189-| transition — soft penalties | Q40 | 45 arms, deployed L1 best |\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-190-| transition — hard bounds | N1, Q54 | per-step geometric bound and global corridor both negative; corridor and penalty are substitutes |\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md:191:| decoder | Q55 | beam average inert; exact optimum has lower cost and ~10× worse RMSE |\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-192-| **state space** | **Q57** | **augmenting the state lowers cost and raises RMSE; the DP declines the freedom it is given** |\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-193-\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-194-Q55 concluded that the remaining lever was *\"redefining the objective so that its optimum is closer to low\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-195-RMSE\"*, and noted that state augmentation was the one untested direction. Q57 tested the most concrete\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-196-instance of it, taken from an independent public architecture, and the objective's optimum moved **further**\n--\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-204-AUC gain does not deliver that content, so this is not a small ask.\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-205-\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-206-## 7. Limits\nreports/q