ian 48.4 ft, max 810 ft\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1991-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md:1992:The degeneracy control is EXACT, so this is not an implementation error. **THE DP INTEGRATES THE\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1993-TRANSITION TERM OVER THE PATH**: a per-step directional prior of a fraction of a grid unit compounds over\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1994-~477 steps into TENS OF FEET of systematic pull -- median 48 ft against a 12 ft RMSE scale. A drift\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1995-estimate that is unbiased in the MEDIAN is therefore not neutral; its per-well noise is amplified by path\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1996-length.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1997-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1998-**SAME FAILURE CLASS AS Q13**, where a coverage-masked emission applied a directional pull that was\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1999-marginally good per row and cumulatively harmful. Q40 is that mechanism on the transition side, now with\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md:2000:a clean degeneracy control and a quantified predictor.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2001-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2002-**PROPOSED STANDING RULE:** *any per-step directional term in a path DP is multiplied by the path length.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2003-Judge estimate quality against the ACCUMULATED pull (|estimate| x steps), not the per-step magnitude; a\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2004-near-zero-mean noisy estimate is actively harmful, not neutral.*\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2005-\n--\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2033-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2034-### Why this was not a repeat of the 07-22 audit\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2035-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2036-That audit tested SINGLE candidates and all failed the 3-well gate, the recorded lesson being that per-well\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2037-gain std (~1.3) far exceeds mean gain, so the 5th percentile is negative for everything. That is a VARIANCE\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md:2038:failure, and averaging is the one operation that reduces variance (Rule #1's transferable class). So Q41\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2039-asked the new question: **does an ensemble of decorrelated members clear the gate every single fails?**\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2040-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2041-Error-correlation with the deployed line identifies the genuinely decorrelated axis: dwt 0.868 and pf 0.831\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2042-vs the structural variants at 0.96-0.97 (near-duplicates -- averaging those is what the task forbids). Both\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2043-classes were included so the distinction is measured, not asserted.\n--\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2179-mechanism rather than by hope.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2180-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2181-**`q55_dp_decoder_averaging` (~10 min).** Beam-average (run_dp keeps K=6 beams but returns only beams[0])\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2182-and soft-min Bellman at temperature gamma. **Precedent that this is not idle: Q21 discovered the deployed\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2183-PF ensemble IS ALREADY a softmax over paths at T=5, sitting at a nested optimum of a 27-member family** --\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md:2184:and the same operator has never been applied to the DP. Requires a degeneracy check that T,gamma -> 0\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-2185-reproduces the current hard-argmin decoder exactl