{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -C 12 'averaging and shrinkage transfer|averaging/shrinkage transfers|fitted per-row|hard selection' reports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md reports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md reports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md | head -n 300\"","aggregated_output":"reports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-67-```\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-68-\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-69-### The smoke inverted at scale — worth recording\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-70-\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-71-On an 8-well smoke the `prior` arm appeared to convert **73.5%** of the oracle headroom. At 40 wells the\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-72-same arm converts **−12.8%**. The smoke's pooled figure was driven by one or two large wins while its own\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-73-per-well statistics already showed the truth (median gain −0.20, 62.5% of wells hurt, 3-well P(gain>0)\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-74-0.48). This is the same failure mode N1 recorded when a 12-well eval manufactured a 25% gain that vanished\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-75-at 40 wells, and it is why the standing rule requires ≥40 wells.\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-76-\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-77-## 5. Why selection loses where averaging wins\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-78-\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md:79:The mechanism is the project's own rule #1: *averaging and shrinkage transfer; hard selection and fitted\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-80-weights do not.*\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-81-\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-82-The PF mean path **is** the averaging. It pools 96 proposals whose spread is median 7.69 ft, and that\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-83-pooling is what makes it robust. A ranker replaces that average with a single bet on one path. With a\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-84-downside of −11.15 against an upside of +3.83 and a selector that is far from oracle-accurate, the\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-85-expected value of the bet is negative — which is precisely what the measurement shows.\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-86-\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-87-This also explains why adding a *better* signal did not rescue it. The problem is not the quality of the\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-88-score used to rank; it is that ranking discards the variance reduction that the mean path provides. A\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-89-better score improves the ranking slightly (`both` beats `prior` by 0.21) without changing the sign.\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-90-\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-91-## 6. Verdict\n--\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-95-\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-96-Both fail. **Q16 closes on its prerequisite without the router being built.**\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-97-\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-98-## What this adds to the ledger\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-99-\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-100-- It **completes** the bound N4 left open. N4 showed error *magnitude* is weakly predictable\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-101-  (R² 0.0736); Q16 shows the *sign* is not predictable at all (R² −0.0802) on the same well-split\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-102-  protocol. Magnitude-without-sign cannot drive a correction — you can know a row is likely wrong and\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-103-  still have no information about which way to move it. This is why the conditional conformal intervals\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-104-  in N4 came out wider than marginal ones, and the two results are now consistent under one explanation.\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-105-- It **generalises** the older post-hoc-residual-correction closure from a specific feature set to the\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-106-  full test-available feature set currently in hand, including the N4 per-well uncertainty features.\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md:107:- It is consistent with **Rule #1** (averaging/shrinkage transfers; fitted per-row structure does not):\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-108-  the only positive-gain regime here is heavy shrinkage toward zero, and the negative R² is fitted\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-109-  structure failing to cross the well boundary.\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-110-\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-111-## Negative results and limits, stated plainly\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-112-\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-113-- The +0.020 ft per-row component is a genuine non-zero effect, not exactly zero. The closure is on\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-114-  *magnitude and reliability*, not on the existence of signal.\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-115-- The learner is `HistGradientBoostingRegressor`, not the exact-split `GradientBoostingRegressor`\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-116-  originally written. Reason recorded below. A different model family (or a much richer feature set)\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-117-  is not excluded by this measurement, but it would have to overcome a **negative** transfer R², not a\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-118-  small positive one.\nreports/q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md-119-- The measurement is on the 760-well train pool. Per the standing 3-well-scale rule, its relevance to\n--\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-776-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-777-The TWH=1 alignment features **alone are the worst arm**; adding them to the prior 14 improves on\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-778-prior-alone (-0.19 vs -0.40) without reaching zero.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-779-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-780-**The smoke inverted at scale, and that is itself the lesson.** On 8 wells the prior arm appeared to\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-781-convert **73.5%** of the oracle headroom; at 40 wells it converts **-12.8%**. Its own per-well statistics\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-782-had already shown the truth on the smoke (median gain -0.20, 62.5% hurt). Same failure mode N1 recorded\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-783-when a 12-well eval manufactured a gain that vanished at 40 — the >=40-well rule earned its place again.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-784-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-785-**Why selection loses where averaging wins.** The PF mean path IS the averaging: it pools 96 proposals\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-786-whose spread is median 7.69 ft, and that pooling is the robustness. A ranker replaces the average with a\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-787-single bet, with downside -11.15 against upside +3.83. This is the project's rule #1 (averaging and\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md:788:shrinkage transfer; hard selection and fitted weights do not), and it explains why a BETTER score did not\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-789-rescue it: the problem is not ranking quality but that ranking discards variance reduction.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-790-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-791-**Closes both shapes in the PF-path line** — generation from a pointwise emission (G3.1/G3.2/N1/Q10) and\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-792-selection among proposals (prior top-K ranker, Q11). Sixth instance of the large-oracle/no-achievable-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-793-margin pattern, and the first where the achievable margin is reliably negative.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-794-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-795-**Banked for any future line:** the oracle best-of-96 is 7.1579, better than deployed 8.8626 — the\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-796-information exists in the path set. The lever is a better *combiner* (a weighting over paths, which\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-797-preserves averaging), not a better ranker.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-798-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-799-Report: `reports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md`. Next queued: `q12_coverage_gated_self_template` (220).\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-800-\n--\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-993-2026-07-28.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-994-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-995-## Round 26 — Q16 honest residual router: CLOSED on its prerequisite\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-996-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-997-`q16_honest_twh1_residual_router` proposed a bounded, confidence-gated residual correction on the\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-998-deployed honest line `54844628`. The direction was resolved at its **prerequisite** rather than by\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-999-building the router: a bounded correction requires the **signed** row residual to be predictable on\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1000-**held-out wells**. It is not.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1001-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1002-`scripts/q16_residual_predictability.py` — 15 test-available features, 3,721,471 rows, 760 wells,\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1003-`GroupKFold(5)` split BY WELL:\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1004-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md:1005:- **signed-residual CV R^2 = -0.0802** (negative: fitted per-row structure ANTI-transfers across the\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1006-  well boundary), corr(pred, actual) 0.0721.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1007-- correction gain profile is **non-monotonic** — +0.0247 at strength 0.25, -0.0248 at 0.5, -0.3398 at 1.0.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1008-  That shape is the signature of a near-zero signal fitted against noise.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1009-- an out-of-fold **constant-only** control (subtract the train-fold mean, no model) yields at most\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1010-  +0.0048, so of the +0.0247 roughly +0.020 ft is genuine per-row signal — **0.23% of an 8.86 ft RMSE**.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1011-- per well it is a coin flip: helped 50.4%, hurt 49.6%, mean gain -0.0034.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1012-- **3-WELL bootstrap: 5th -0.9333, 50th +0.0072, 95th +0.8933, P(gain>0) 0.5078.** The +-0.9 ft spread at\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1013-  competition scale is ~40x the +0.02 ft effect.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1014-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1015-**GATE FAILS BOTH CONDITIONS** (materially positive R^2; 3-well 5th pct > 0). No submission, no quota.\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md-1016-\nreports/rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.