t the margin is grid-fragile.\n54-    \n55-    LIVE REFRESH. origin/main (Marc0823) moved: a589fa8 \"Add reproducible public 6.626 ROGII kernel\" —\n56-    recorded only, 6.626 is worse than our best own-account public 6.563 (54922806), no decision taken.\n57-    55064411 remains PENDING (~5.5h) with kernel status COMPLETE/failureMessage null, so the stall stays\n58-    Kaggle-side; not resubmitted. No local GPU on this box (nvidia-smi absent).\n59-    \n60-    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n--\n323-+and α=0.3 the AUC rises 40× more and the DP barely moves. **The DP responds to how much literal truth is\n324-+mixed into the emission, not to the emission's discriminative AUC.**\n325-+\n326-+This also explains the mechanism cleanly. Changing TWH alters the emission's *shape* over the typewell,\n327-+not only its discriminative quality; Q10's 1.04 RMSE gain came from that structural change, and attaching\n328-+it to the accompanying AUC movement produced a slope that does not generalise. The α-sweep isolates pure\n329-+discriminative quality at fixed structure, and it is nearly flat.\n330-+\n331-+**New standing rule (proposed):** *emission AUC is not a valid proxy for DP trajectory quality; an\n332-+emission change must be validated on its DP output, not on AUC or any pointwise emission metric.* This\n333:+subsumes the rule Q13 produced (a pointwise emission metric is not a valid proxy when the modification\n334-+carries a directional bias) — Q13 and Q17 are two instances of the same failure, now with the mechanism\n335-+measured on a continuous axis.\n336-+\n337-+## 6. Verdict against Q17's own steps\n338-+\n339-+- **Step 2 (HOLD if no real signal):** Q11 and Q13 are negative. Q10's signal is real but its training\n340-+  premise is now measured and does not hold: the quantity a learned scorer would improve (AUC) is ~11×\n341-+  less effective than assumed and is decoupled from the objective.\n342-+- **Step 3 (prepare a tiny Kaggle GPU smoke):*