 after N1's 12-well set and Q10's grid sensitivity.\"}\n100- {\"id\": \"q22_frontier_hedgeoff_score_response\", \"path\": \"prompts/q22_frontier_hedgeoff_score_response.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 520, \"queue_reason\": \"Fires when 55064411 lands; Q19 pre-registered the reading, so it is decisive rather than exploratory. Absorbs q32 score-watcher.\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T04:20:00Z\", \"result\": \"Discharged early by q33, because 55064411 landed (public 6.695) during that round and the standing rules require recording a landed score immediately. PRE-REGISTERED READING APPLIED, WITH A CORRECTION: Q19 framed the threshold against 6.563, but 54922806 is a DIFFERENT branch (teammate overlap-ON); 55064411 was diff-verified against the kernel producing 54968060 (6.643), so the controlled contrast is 6.695 vs 6.643 = +0.052 -- INSIDE the ~0.115 config-variance floor and inside Q18's coin-flip band. Neither pre-registered branch fires; the honest outcome is a third: THE BIMODAL HEDGE IS NOT LOAD-BEARING ON PUBLIC IN EITHER DIRECTION, and the public score does not adjudicate Q14's local finding. SECOND CORRECTION: the my0705 datapoint (6.568->6.520 = -0.048) is also inside the floor, so Q19 overstated it as support; the 'hedge tuned to public wells' hypothesis is neither confirmed nor refuted. Q14's LOCAL measurement (+2.0 ft applied to a well whose residual was already -0.19) stands untouched. 55064411 at 6.695 is our WORST frontier candidate on public and enters no slot; the final-pair recommendation is unchanged.\"}\n101--{\"id\": \"q23_frontier_stage_localizer\", \"path\": \"prompts/q23_frontier_stage_localizer.md\", \"status\": \"deferred\", \"priority\": 330, \"deferred_reason\": \"Needs its own frontier full run, and Q19 showed the whole 6.2-6.7 band is largely one family spread while Q18 showed the 0.080 deciding slot 1 is unresolvable at 3-well scale. Stage localisation on public has low expected value.\", \"deferred_at\": \"2026-07-29T03:05: