in flight.\n--\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md:1:# Q18 — final-pair stress test: the gap that decides slot 1 is not resolvable at 3-well scale\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-2-\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-3-Date: 2026-07-29\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-4-Task: `q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress` (`requires_gpu=false`, `can_submit=false`, `max_submit_cost=0`)\n--\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-139-| family correlation | unchanged — locally measured pred-corr ≥ 0.99996 within the honest/frontier local set; family diversity stays a 0/1 term, since correlation is unavailable for teammate outputs and a missing value must be neutral, not worst-case |\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-140-| provenance risk | narrowed by the G1.3 audit: **one** prediction-affecting third-party dataset (`fleongg/rogii-claude-models-pub`), worth ≈0.047 as a **joint** bound with the bimodal hedge |\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-141-| OOF support | `54844628` remains the only 760-well nested-OOF + bootstrap candidate |\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md:142:| public→private transfer (N4) | OOF on the 3 test wells 4.756 vs public 7.891 = **1.659×**; OOF-derived bounds are not leaderboard bounds. **Extended by §6:** not only the level but the *ranking* is unstable at 3-well scale |\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-143-| private score visibility | **none** — `privateScore` empty for every submission; never used |\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-144-\nreports/q18_public_leaderboard_family_stress_2026-07-29.md-145-## 9. Verdict\n--\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-30-row subsampling), so it is test-available. `l1` is the `μ=0` special case of `drift`, making that arm a\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-31-clean single-factor test of *\"does the DP wrongly assume zero drift is free?\"*\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-32-\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md:33:Protocol per the standing rules: splits **by well**, 40 eval wells (same split seed as Q10/Q17), every\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-34-parameter chosen **nested**. Validation is on **DP output only**, never a pointwise emission metric —\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-35-Q17's rule.\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-36-\n--\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-108-drift prior is the same mechanism on the transition side, now with a clean degeneracy control and a\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-109-quantified predictor.\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-110-\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md:111:**Proposed standing rule:** *any per-step directional term in a path DP is multiplied by the path length.\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-112-Estimate quality must be judged against the accumulated pull (|estimate| × steps), not against the\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-113-per-step magnitude; a near-zero-mean noisy estimate is actively harmful, not neutral.*\nreports/q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md-114-\n--\nreports/q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy_2026-07-30.md-62-size of **152 wells, not 744,000 rows**. The apparent taxonomy is well-level sampling noise dressed as\nreports/q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy_2026-07-30.md-63-segment structure.\nreports/q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy_2026-07-30.md-64-\nreports/q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy_2026-07-30.md:65:**Proposed standing rule:** *when segmenting residuals by a WELL-level feature, the effective n is the\nreports/q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy_2026-07-30.md-66-number of wells in the bin, not the number of rows. Compare any observed spread against σ_well/√n_wells\nreports/q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy_2026-07-30.md-67-before treating it as structure.*\nreports/q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy_2026-07-30.md-68-\n--\nreports/q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup_2026-07-29.md-115-it to the accompanying AUC movement produced a slope that does not generalise. The α-sweep isolates pure\nreports/q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup_2026-07-29.md-116-discriminative quality at fixed structure, and it is nearly flat.\nreports/q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup_2026-07-29.md-117-\nreports/q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup_2026-07-29.md:118:**New standing rule (proposed):** *emission AUC is not a valid proxy for DP trajectory quality; an\nreports/q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup_2026-07-29.md-119-emission change must be validated on its DP output, not on AUC or any pointwise emission metric.* This\nreports/q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup_2026-07-29.md-120-subsumes the rule Q13 produced (a pointwise emission metric is not a valid proxy when the modification\nreports/q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup_2026-07-29.md-121-carries a directional bias) — Q13 and Q17 are two instances of the same failure, now with the mechanism\n--\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-72-same arm converts **−12.8%**. The smoke's pooled figure was driven by one or two large wins while its own\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-73-per-well statistics already showed the truth (median gain −0.20, 62.5% of wells hurt, 3-well P(gain>0)\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-74-0.48). This is the same failure mode N1 recorded when a 12-well eval manufactured a 25% gain that vanished\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md:75:at 40 wells, and it is why the standing rule requires ≥40 wells.\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-76-\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-77-## 5. Why selection loses where averaging wins\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-78-\n","exit_