by having a shorter prefix, which inflates the\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:33:correlation. The deployment-honest pairing is: signal from the **truncated** run (that is what inference\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-34-can compute), target from the **full-prefix** run (that is the error a correction must fix).\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-35-\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-36-## Result (30 train wells, PF forward, both cut fractions)\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-37-\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-38-```\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-39-CUT = 0.70   held-out median 493 rows | toe median 5182 rows\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:40:  [confounded]  corr(bias_hold, bias_toe from the SAME truncated run) = +0.6589  -> 43.4%\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-41-  [deployment]  corr(bias_hold, bias_toe from the FULL-prefix run)    = +0.1862  ->  3.5%\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-42-  corr(drift_hold, drift_toe) = +0.1431 -> 2.0%\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-43-  best scalar a=0.408: toe-bias std 7.632 -> 7.500; variance removed 3.4% (IN-SAMPLE upper bound)\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-44-\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-45-CUT = 0.50\\n--\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-73-\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-74-`54844628` is unchanged and remains the slot-2 recommendation under all three criteria.\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-75-\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-76-### Transferable finding (worth carrying into any future calibration work)\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-77-\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:78:**Never measure a calibration signal and its target on the same truncated run.** Doing so inflated the\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-79-apparent correlation by 3–4× here (0.659 vs 0.186; 0.376 vs 0.074). Any prefix-calibration design — ours\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md:80:or the frontier's — must pair a truncated-run signal with a full-prefix target, or it will report a\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-81-signal that does not exist at inference. This is consistent with what the frontier's own calibration does\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-82-in practice: G1.2 found its selected `balanced` profile applied `alpha = 0.0` (no movement at all), and\\nreports/g35_honest_prefix_calibration_2026-07-28.md-83-`54990075` showed the post-SP45 stages as a whole are only mildly useful on public.\\n--\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-91-## 5. What this changes\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-92-\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-93-1. **`54968060` is validated as a genuine no-retrieval frontier run** — the slot-2 candidacy rests on\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-94-   solid ground.\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-95-2. **The frontier's strength is concentrated in SP45 + PF/beam**, not in the later refinement stages,\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md:96:   two of which are inert here and one of which is proxy-negative.\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-97-3. **A concrete round-2 candidate exists**: an *SP45-projection-only* variant. Audit:\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-98-   HARD PASS, proxy RMSE **2.581** (best of any candidate), rmse **1.809 vs `54968060`** → non-homogeneous.\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-99-   Its information value is that it tests directly whether the frontier's post-SP45 stages help or hurt\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-100-   on the leaderboard — which decides which frontier variant should hold slot 2.\\nreports/frontier_oof_component_validation_2026-07-26.md-101-   **Caveat (§3): the proxy saturates, so its 0.68 ft proxy advantage may not transfer.** It is worth one\\n--\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-26-\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-27-## Consequence for the final slot — `54968060` may be more than a diagnostic\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-28-\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-29-Earlier framing (D1) treated the overlap-OFF frontier as \\\"corr 1.0 with honest → equal under H-hidden,\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-30-diagnostic only\\\". D3 corrects this: on the local truth space the overlap-OFF frontier is **better** than\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md:31:our honest slot. So under **H-hidden** (novel wells, overlap inert) the frontier's non-overlap stack\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-32-could **outperform** `54844628`, making `54968060` a *candidate* H-hidden hedge, not merely a diagnostic.\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-33-\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-34-**Caveat (decisive):** this is measured against train-copy TVT, and 2026-07-22 established that local\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-35-truth-space accuracy does not predict the leaderboard at the ≲0.1 scale (our own 54878409 was better\\nreports/frontier_vs_honest_error_decorrelation_2026-07-25.md-36-locally, worse on public). So \\\"frontier better locally\\\" is suggestive, not conclusive. The pending public\\n--\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-2-\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-3-Round 2 of the rotation pipeline. **Submitted: ref `54990075` (PENDING).** Today 1/5 used, 4 remaining.\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-4-\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-5-## What it is\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-6-\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md:7:The frontier notebook truncated after its **SP45 projection** stage: a final cell writes\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-8-`sp45_projection_submission.csv` as `submission.csv`, with row-count and finiteness asserts so the patch\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-9-cannot silently no-op. Built on the overlap-OFF notebook, so **retrieval/overlap stays OFF** — this is a\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-10-no-lookup candidate by construction.\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-11-\\nreports/g21_sp45_only_2026-07-26.md-12-It removes the frontier's post-SP45 stages: learned-trajectory blend (w=0.60), visible-prefix\\n--\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-14-\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-15-## The one question that dominates variant value: H-visible vs H-hidden\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-16-\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-17-- **H-visible** (public/private = row splits of the 3 visible wells): overlap + prefix-calibration are\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-18-  legitimate and the frontier family's public advantage carries to private.\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md:19:- **H-hidden** (rerun scores novel wells): overlap goes inert (no train duplicate), prefix-calibration\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-20-  still applies (any well has a known heel), and the family reverts toward its base PF/beam quality.\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-21-\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-22-The variant queue is designed to *probe* this without needing organizer confirmation.\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-23-\\nreports/kaiwalya_frontier_variant_queue_2026-07-24.md-24-## Queue — each: smoke (FAST) → full → judge\\n--\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-29-As the transition penalty rises, the DP **converges toward the flat-anchor baseline from above and never\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-30-crosses it**. At `LAM=60` the path search is still slightly worse than simply holding the anchor TVT\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-31-constant (13.638 vs 13.278), and the whole family sits far above the honest pipeline's ~8.86 ft.\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-32-\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-33-The reading is unambiguous: **every amount of GR-emission influence makes the prediction worse than\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md:34:ignoring GR entirely.** The optimum of this formulation is the degenerate one.\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-35-\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-36-The beam adds nothing either: top-1 → oracle top-8 improves by 0.035 / 0.107 / 0.559 ft across the three\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-37-settings. The K paths are near-duplicates, so a ranker over them (the earlier top-K line) would have\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-38-nothing to choose between — consistent with that line's own negative result.\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-39-\\n--\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-51-\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-52-## Disposition\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-53-\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-54-**G3.1 closed on evidence.** One repair iteration (raising the transition penalty) was used to confirm\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-55-the diagnosis rather than to rescue the result; the direction is closed because its optimum is the\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md:56:degenerate flat path, not because of tuning cost. No Kaggle quota was spent.\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-57-\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-58-Any future revival would need a formulation where the emission term is **not pointwise** — e.g. matching\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-59-a whole trajectory segment against the typewell with an explicit motion model, which is what the existing\\nreports/g31_heatmap_topk_2026-07-26.md-60-PF already implements.\\n--\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-47-variance-reduction win, and per the 2026-07-22 finding it could not be validated at 3-well scale anyway.\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-48-**D1 verdict: no distinct H-hidden improvement from blending — the two lines converge.**\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-49-\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-50-## The decisive final-selection consequence\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-51-\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md:52:Under **H-hidden** (private = novel wells, no train duplicates), the overlap override is inert, so the\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-53-frontier family reduces to its non-overlap path — which is **corr 1.0 with our honest `54844628`**. So on\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-54-novel wells the 6.5 frontier and our honest slot predict essentially the same thing. **The entire 6.5→7.9\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-55-public gap is the overlap lookup on the visible wells.** This makes the two-slot hedge exact:\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-56-\\nreports/kaiwalya_overlap_off_ablation_2026-07-25.md-57-- **H-visible**: the overlap-ON 6.5 family wins (overlap returns near-truth). Slot `54922806` (6.563).\\n--\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-66-**+0.9194**. It is a re-weighting of the same field, not a decorrelated second source. The two-field\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-67-combination being *worse* than either alone (−0.2298) confirms the redundancy — there is nothing\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-68-independent for a second coefficient to buy.\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-69-\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-70-Caveat on absolute values: this subset is **ungated** and easy (base 7.39 vs the global 9.30), so the\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md:71:structural field is net-negative here where the deployed gated version is positive. Only the *relative*\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-72-comparison and the correlation are informative.\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-73-\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-74-## Disposition\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-75-\\nreports/l5_decorrelated_forward_smoke_2026-07-21.md-76-- The GR-weighted variant is not a decorrelated third source. It could be re-examined later as a minor\\n--\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-55-\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-56-## Disposition\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-57-\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-58-A3/A4/A5 are **informational, HOLD**. They confirm the 6.5 family's visible-well output is dominated by\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-59-the overlap override; the model-package correction is a small bounded top-up; bimodal and\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md:60:prefix-aggressiveness are inert on the scored wells. The one ablation that reveals the H-hidden-relevant\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-61-(non-overlap) behavior is **A2 overlap-OFF**, which requires its own run (no \\\"before overlap\\\" intermediate\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-62-exists) — smoke in progress. None of A3/A4/A5 is submittable: each is a homogeneous intermediate of the\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-63-already-submitted family.\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-64-\\nreports/kaiwalya_modelpkg_prefix_bimodal_ablations_2026-07-25.md-65----\\n--\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-2-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-3-Autopilot task `n1_geometry_bounded_alignment` (`requires_gpu=false`, `can_submit=false`,\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-4-`max_submit_cost=0`). Script: `scripts/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment.py`. Logs:\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-5-`reports/logs/n1_{geometry_bounded,geometry_bounded_lowlam,nested}_2026-07-28.log`.\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-6-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md:7:**Result: negative. The band is not inert — it binds 83–91% of transitions — but it does not improve the\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-8-alignment DP.** A large apparent gain on 12 wells did not survive expansion to 40, and under nested\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-9-hyper-parameter selection the whole DP family fails to beat the flat anchor. That last point also\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-10-qualifies a number recorded in G3.2 earlier today.\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-11-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-12-## 1. The constraint, and why it is not a hyper-parameter\\n--\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-58-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-59-After the fix the band binds 83–97%, as the geometry implies.\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-60-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-61-## 3. What the sweep showed — and why it is not the answer\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-62-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md:63:Control check: the flat-anchor baseline on the 12-well eval set reproduces G3.2's recorded **13.103**\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-64-exactly, confirming the same eval wells. The scorer retrains to AUC **0.7096** (G3.2 recorded 0.7242;\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-65-the original left its pair-sampling RNG unseeded, so the model is not bit-reproducible — the internal\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-66-arm-to-arm comparison is the valid one, and the G3.2 numbers are an external reference).\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-67-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-68-**12 eval wells, low λ** — this looked like a large win:\\n--\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-89-flat-anchor 12.722\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-90-```\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-91-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-92-`bounded 8°` at lam=2 goes from **9.412** on 12 wells to **15.569** on 40. The best arm on 40 wells is the\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-93-**unbounded control**, and every geometry-aware arm is worse. The 9.412 was a minimum selected over 20\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md:94:configurations on a 12-well sample — the project's recorded failure mode (*a parameter sweep is not a\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-95-validation*), and the reason the sweep was not accepted as the result.\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-96-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-97-## 4. Nested validation — the deciding test\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-98-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-99-Configuration chosen on one half of the eval wells, scored on the disjoint other half, both ways:\\n--\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-124-optimum, and the optimum it protects is worse than the tuned unbounded arm. Recorded because a future\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-125-formulation that needs a weak regulariser for other reasons can rely on the bound to stay physical.\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-126-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-127-## 6. Verdict\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-128-\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md:129:- The band is **binding** (83–91% of transitions), so the constraint is active, not inert.\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-130-- It does **not** improve the DP: on 40 wells every geometry-aware arm is worse than the unbounded\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-131-  control, and nested selection never chooses one.\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-132-- The DP family as a whole does not beat the flat anchor under nested selection (13.644 vs 12.722,\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-133-  beating flat on 37.5% of wells), so it remains far from the deployed honest line (~8.86).\\nreports/n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md-134-- Task step 5 (\\\"do not scale up unless the band produces a clear improvement over 12.527\\\") is not met.\\n--\\nreports/n5_typewell_fingerprint_families_2026-07-28.md-45-\\nreports/n5_typewell_fingerprint_families_2026-07-28.md-46-## 2. Correction to M3\\nreports/n5_typewell_fingerprint_families_2026-07-28.md-47-\\nreports/n5_typewell_fingerprint_families_2026-07-28.md-48-`new_direction_search` M3 hashed whole typewell files and reported **0 of 3 test wells matching any train\\nreports/n5_typewell_fingerprint_families_2026-07-28.md-49-typewell**, concluding that exact grouping was unusable. That measurement was correct but its framing\\nreports/n5_typewell_fingerprint_families_2026-07-