 it robust. A ranker replaces that average with a single bet on one path. With a\\nreports/q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md-84-downside of −11.15 against an upside of +3.83 and a selector that is far from oracle-accurate, the\\n--\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-61-gs = float(np.clip(np.nanstd(kn.GR.fillna(0).values - tw_at_k), 10., 60.)) * 1.3    # theirs\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-62-```\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-63-\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-64-`gs` is the GR noise sigma in the PF likelihood (`d = (gr − expected) / gs`). Multiplying it widens the\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-65-assumed measurement noise and flattens the likelihood — a **shrinkage/regularisation** change, which is\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md:66:the class Rule #1 records as transferring. That is why it earned a measurement rather than dismissal.\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-67-\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-68-Note this corrects an intermediate hypothesis of mine: an earlier constant-diff appeared to show a\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-69-`SUBMISSION_PROFILE = contact_gated_anchor` difference. That diff had concatenated **markdown** with code.\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-70-In code all three notebooks run `'vp_balanced_modelpkg_005'`, and the upstream comment block explicitly\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-71-records that `contact_gated_anchor*` are *\\\"diagnostic ablations … [that] have underperformed\\\"*. No kernel\\n--\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-146-Recorded now so the interpretation is not chosen after seeing the number.\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-147-\\nreports/q19_external_solution_refresh_2026-07-29.md-148-## 5. Queued follow-ups (Q19 allows 1–3)\\nreports/q