er_averaging_2026-07-30.md-86-\\nreports/q55_dp_decoder_averaging_2026-07-30.md:87:**Decoder averaging is closed.** The beam average is inert (six paths agreeing to 0.1 ft); the soft-min\\nreports/q55_dp_decoder_averaging_2026-07-30.md-88-posterior, which is the correct and general form of the operator, concentrates on an optimum that is worse\\nreports/q55_dp_decoder_averaging_2026-07-30.md-89-than the beam's answer. Both fail the gate.\\nreports/q55_dp_decoder_averaging_2026-07-30.md-90-\\nreports/q55_dp_decoder_averaging_2026-07-30.md-91-**More broadly:** the alignment line is now closed on the emission side (Q17: AUC decoupled from DP\\nreports/q55_dp_decoder_averaging_2026-07-30.md-92-quality), the transition side (Q40 soft penalties, N1 per-step geometric bounds, Q54 global corridors), and\\n--\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-65-  off-gate      : median 0.0000\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-66-```\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-67-\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-68-**The stage is now fully characterised by (meta gate, W = 0.15)**, so substituting a smoothed PF into it is\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-69-a clean one-factor change. This also corrects a latent trap for any future round: the aligned frame's\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md:70:`nnb`/`closest_surv` columns are *not* the deployed gate and silently disagree on 6 wells.\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-71-\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-72-## 3. What the producer is computing, and why NS=64\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-73-\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-74-Q56 saved only per-well SSE, so it cannot support a re-fit; the missing artifact is the row-level PF\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-75-prediction. The producer emits `pf_fwd` and `pf_sm` per toe row, aligned to `aligned_preds.npz` by\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md:76:(well, ridx) with the same `ridx`-equality and truth-equality assertions Q36/Q56 use.\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-77-\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-78-**NS = 64, the deployed configuration.** Q36 and Q56 both ran NS=32 to bound wall-time and both had to carry\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-79-a caveat about it. Beyond removing that caveat, NS=64 buys a second control for free: the stored `pf` column\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-80-in `aligned_preds.npz` *is* the deployed NS=64 forward PF, so `pf_fwd` can be checked directly against it.\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-81-The evaluator prints that comparison (§1 of its output) before using anything.\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-82-\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md:83:The smoother, the trellis twin and its byte-for-byte degeneracy check are **imported unchanged** from\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md:84:`scripts/q56_pf_backward_smoothing.py` rather than re-implemented, and the producer re-runs the degeneracy\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-85-assertion itself so the artifact carries its own proof:\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-86-\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-87-```\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md:88:degeneracy control: array_equal(deployed run_particle_filter, trellis twin) = True\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-89-```\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-90-\\nreports/q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md-91-Producer smoke (Di