eports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-34-\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md:35:## 2. The first smoke was inert — and the cause is arithmetic, not a bug\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-36-\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md:37:The activation diagnostic (mandatory, after N1 and Q54 each nearly reported an inert constraint as \\\"no\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-38-effect\\\") caught it immediately:\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-39-\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-40-```\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-41-ndip / nu / mu      dip!=0   dip chg   mean|dip|  accum pull   path dev  truth dev\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-42-1 / 0 / 60            0.0%      0.0%       0.000         0.0        3.1       16.3\\n--\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-87-so it is the one kept at resolution.\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-88-\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-89-**One in-flight change, recorded rather than silently made.** The first launch used `ndip ∈ {1, 5, 9}`. Its\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-90-`ndip=9` timing block alone ran past 4.5 min on 8 wells, projecting **60+ min** for that arm — and both\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-91-this sweep and Q56's 760-well run share a **2-core** box, so that time comes directly out of the round that\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md:92:has the only live positive result in the rotation. The sweep was stopped (by verified PID, not `pkill -f`)\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-93-and relaunched with `ndip ∈ {1, 3, 5}`: `ndip=3` costs ~0.36× the `ndip=5` arm, so the three-point width\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-94-ladder survives at roughly a tenth of the cost. What is given up is the widest dose point; what it buys is\\nreports/q57_di