e_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-196-instance of it, taken from an independent public architecture, and the objective's optimum moved **further**\\n--\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-204-AUC gain does not deliver that content, so this is not a small ask.\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-205-\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-206-## 7. Limits\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-207-\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-208-- One emission (TWH=1), one scorer seed, the Q10/Q40/Q54 split seed. 8 wells in the smoke, 40 in the sweep.\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md:209:- **The activation diagnostic is well 0 of each run only**, and the two runs have different eval sets\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-210-  (`MAXW_TRAIN` differs), so their \\\"well 0\\\" is a different well. That is exactly how the smoke misled the\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-211-  first draft of §4 — its well kept the dip nearly off, the sweep's well switches it on 42-46% of the time.\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-212-  The per-well diagnostic is indicative, not a population statement, and the correction is left visible in\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-213-  §4 rather than quietly rewritten.\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-214-- The λ grid is reduced to `mu = 60` (§3). A dip effect that only appears at a λ far from the TVT-only\\n--\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-216-  no interaction that changed the optimum's location.\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-217-- The dip grid is unit-spaced in grid units (~1 ft) per DP step and centred on 0; a finer or asymmetric dip\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-218-  grid was not tested.\\nreports/q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md-219-- `DSC = 1.0`, so `nu` is directly on the z-scored emission scale. That is why 