t.py-156-        \\\"\\\",\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-157-        \\\"=== quota_estimate_utc ===\\\",\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-158-        f\\\"used={quota_used}/5 remaining={max(0, 5 - quota_used)}/5\\\",\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-159-        \\\"\\\",\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-160-        \\\"=== local_processes ===\\\",\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-161-        run_shell(\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-162-            \\\"ps -eo pid,ppid,stat,etime,cmd | \\\"\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-163-            \\\"egrep 'codex|claude|kaggle|papermill|jupyter|python|ipykernel' | \\\"\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py:164:            \\\"grep -v egrep | cut -c1-220 | head -40\\\",\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-165-            30,\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-166-        ),\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-167-    ]\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-168-    return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(parts)\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-169-\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-170-\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-171-def mark_current_task_finished(state: dict, queue: list[dict], js: dict) -> bool:\\nscripts/codex_autopilot.py-172-    task_id = state.get(\\\"current_task_id\\\")\\n--\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-29-   byte-identical file.\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-30-\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-31-Required execution — deliberately bounded, this is a **documentation** task:\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-32-\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-33-1. Write `reports/measurement_traps_ledger.md`: one entry per trap, each with (a) the symptom as it first\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-34-   appeared, (b) the mechanism, (c) **the specific check that would have caught it**, (d) the round and the\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-35-   report where it was found. Cite the four above and sweep the earlier reports for any others already\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-36-   recorded as project rules (Rule #1, Rule #3, the Q17 / Q40 / Q42 rules, N1's and Q54's inert-constraint\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md:37:   trap, the `pkill -f` self-match, `python3` block-buffering, `head` SIGPIPE, the `open(path,'w')`\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-38-   truncation that `scripts/append_section.py` exists to prevent).\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-39-2. Convert the checks into a short **pre-flight list** a future round can actually run, ordered by how often\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-40-   the trap has actually occurred, not by how severe it sounds.\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-41-3. State plainly which traps are **already** enforced in code (e.g. `append_section.append`, the anchored-\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-42-   insertion + `array_equal` degeneracy pattern from Q56, the `ridx`/truth-equality assertions in\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-43-   `q36`/`q56`/`q58`) and which are only conventions a reader must remember. The second list is the useful\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-44-   output.\\n.claude/autopilot/prompts/q28_measurement_traps_ledger.md-45-4. **No new measurement, no CPU-heavy run, no submission.** If it cannot be written from existing reports,\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n.claude/autopilot/codex_jobs/codex_20260731T124220Z_q28_measurement_traps_ledger/codex.jsonl:50:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"rg -n -i 'sigpipe|broken pipe' . --hidden --glob '\\\"'!*.ipynb'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!*.csv'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!*.npz'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!*.jsonl'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!reports/logs/q45_pulled/**'\\\"' | head -n 2