{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git diff -- .claude/autopilot/queue.jsonl .claude/autopilot/state.json .claude/autopilot/sent_log.jsonl | sed -n '1,280p'; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/.claude/autopilot/queue.jsonl b/.claude/autopilot/queue.jsonl\nindex 472891a..d711d3f 100644\n--- a/.claude/autopilot/queue.jsonl\n+++ b/.claude/autopilot/queue.jsonl\n@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@\n {\"id\": \"q46_submission_asset_inventory\", \"path\": \"prompts/q46_submission_asset_inventory.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 650, \"queue_reason\": \"Build final reproducibility and winner-obligation asset map; mark known/inferred/missing/inaccessible fields.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T23:44:00Z\", \"handle\": \"cb20d18c\", \"prompt_hash\": \"2c4848364af1a69bffbcbf5121f6a9a6ec3ee2fa0d743730c939f2b32e9cb17d\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-29T23:57:00Z\", \"result\": \"DONE. No submission, quota 0/5. Artifacts produced: reports/submission_outputs/ (5 verified submission files + provenance README). METHOD IMPROVEMENT over Q38: the submission object's `url` field carries the kernel slug AND scriptVersionId directly (e.g. /code/joezzzzz/rogii-frontier-hedgeoff-full?scriptVersionId=338650633), so all seven candidates are KNOWN rather than inferred, including our own side which Q38 left implicit. INVENTORY: 54922806 leemarc223 rogii-public-pf-frontier-rerun-20260723 svid 337355891 (no repo commit); 54968060 joezzzzz rogii-kaiwalya-overlap-off-full 337787958 commit 9857c3a; 54844628 joezzzzz rogii-struct-field-blend-codex 336599680 commit d972986; 55064411 joezzzzz rogii-frontier-hedgeoff-full 338650633 commit f491826; 54990075 joezzzzz rogii-frontier-sp45-only-full 337982098 commit dd4e79e; 54896975 leemarc223 rogii-kaiwalya-public-tvt-6-626-repro 337097140; 54923144 leemarc223 rogii-gr-sigma-1-0-frontier-20260723 337362917. All on team 'lee Marc223', 4 joezzzzz / 3 leemarc223. All four parsed commits verified present via git cat-file; the three teammate submissions carry no commit, expected since they were not run from this repo, and the pulled package is the substitute. OUTPUTS RETRIEVED AND VERIFIED via api.kernels_output(): all seven pass 14,151 rows / id set equal / id order equal / all finite. Five archived, each tied to its submission by a number recorded AT SUBMISSION TIME: 54990075 rmse 1.640 vs 54968060 (its description says 1.640), 55064411 rmse 1.756 (says 1.756), 54968060 rmse 3.105 and 2.537 (says 3.1 and 2.54), 54896975 sha256 prefix b192d3 (says 'SHA b192d3'). THE FINDING: 54922806, 54896975 and 54923144 scored 6.563/6.669/6.678 yet their kernels' currently-retrievable outputs are BYTE-IDENTICAL (b192d3f348ae = 54896975's recorded SHA). Three scores cannot come from one prediction file, so the copies under the other two refs are POST-SUBMISSION RE-RUNS; they were deleted rather than archived, because a file named 54922806_submission.csv that is not 54922806's output is worse than no file. THIS ANSWERS Q38'S UNANSWERED QUESTION WITH EVIDENCE, without needing a reply: at least two teammate kernels have been edited or re-run since submission. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE SLOTS: the submitted artifact of the SCORE-FIRST SLOT-1 CANDIDATE is not archived and cannot be fetched by API (kernels_output serves only the latest version); it is one owner UI action away (Version history -> scriptVersionId 337355891 -> Output). Does NOT change the recommendation -- Q44 already found the two slot-1 options tied on measurement with ownership as tie-breaker -- but creates a clean asymmetry: if slot 1 is 54968060 every asset for both slots is already archived and verified locally; if it is 54922806, one owner action is outstanding. LIMIT RECORDED: dataset_sources is read from the CURRENT kernel version, and since at least two teammate kernels have moved, their submitted-version dataset lists are inferred, not known. Also recorded so a future round does not misread it: a submission object's total_bytes (~31 MB) is the OUTPUT BUNDLE, not the CSV (~464 KB).\"}\n {\"id\": \"q47_final_selection_ui_checklist\", \"path\": \"prompts/q47_final_selection_ui_checklist.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 660, \"queue_reason\": \"Final selection is separate from submitting and costs no quota; owner needs exact operational checklist.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T23:59:00Z\", \"handle\": \"3a2fed70\", \"prompt_hash\": \"1c910696ad09e71cae3901a1efad75bc82cb3f9ebd242ef3c8729e9824f64539\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-30T00:08:00Z\", \"result\": \"DONE. No submission, no selection made, quota 0/5. MECHANISM PROBED, NOT ASSUMED: the Kaggle API has NO final-selection endpoint (the only selection-shaped symbols are the private _select_models_interactively helper for model uploads, competition_leaderboard_*, and competition_team_submissions(team_id:int)) and ApiSubmission has NO `selected`/`is_final` field (date, description, error_description, file_name, private_score, public_score, ref, status, submitted_by, submitted_by_ref, team_name, total_bytes, url), nor does team_public_submission_fields (['id','dateSubmitted','publicScore']). TWO CONSEQUENCES: the selection can only be made in a browser by the owner, AND its state CANNOT BE VERIFIED PROGRAMMATICALLY -- so no future report may claim 'selection verified' without a screenshot or the owner's word. THE HEADLINE: 54844628 ranks 9th of our 20 submissions by public score, so BOTH plausible auto-selection rules EXCLUDE IT -- 'best public 2' gives 54922806+54968060 and 'most recent 2' gives 55064411+54990075, and both of those pairs are FRONTIER-ONLY with family diversity 0. Kaggle's rules language confirms a Final Submission is 'the Submission selected by the user, OR AUTOMATICALLY SELECTED BY KAGGLE in the event not selected by the user', so an automatic selection WILL happen; the exact criterion is unverified and the checklist is deliberately built so that it does not matter. COST OF THE DEFAULT, from Q44's measured pair values: the recommended diverse pair is 6.1818 mean / 8.5017 p95 versus the best-public default at 6.5783 / 9.3671, i.e. +0.3965 mean and +0.8654 tail -- FIVE TIMES the entire slot-1 dispute (<=0.077 ft), avoidable by two clicks at zero quota. So the manual selection is the highest-value zero-cost action left in the competition, and doing nothing does not preserve the recommended pair, it discards it. CHECKLIST DELIVERED: submissions-page URL, team view (teammate rows only appear there), match rows by REF ID not score since several are within 0.03, the 'Use for Final Score' control is a row toggle or a three-dot menu item whose LABEL WORDING CHANGES between UI revisions so look for the control mentioning 'final', verify the '2 of 2 selected' count, un-mark any stale third selection, hard-refresh and re-confirm, then record the selection with a UTC timestamp in the ledger. DEADLINES: hard 2026-08-05 23:59 UTC = 2026-08-06 07:59 Beijing; recommended completion 2026-08-04 12:00 UTC = 20:00 Beijing. POLICY TABLE: score-first 54922806+54844628; diversity-first 54922806 or 54968060 + 54844628; ownership/provenance-first 54968060+54844628 (recommended default); all three put 54844628 in SLOT 2. FALLBACK now concrete rather than hypothetical, per Q46: 54922806's submitted artifact is unarchivable by API, so 54968060+54844628 costs +0.0013 ft in the evidence-supported cell, keeps both slots on our own account, and both artifacts are archived with git commits in this repo; if 54922806 is still preferred, one owner action remains (Version history -> scriptVersionId 337355891 -> Output), which is a DISCLOSURE requirement and NOT a blocker on the selection itself. NO CLI OR SCREENSHOT ALTERNATIVE EXISTS and that is recorded as a limitation rather than papered over with an invented UI walkthrough. LIMITS: the competition's own /rules page is behind a login wall and could not be retrieved, so the rules quote is Kaggle's general competition-rules language via search -- the same gap Q30 recorded, still open. Rank drift noted: 1277 (Q19) -> 1339 (Q45) -> 1354 now, with our own score unchanged.\"}\n {\"id\": \"q48_reopen_deferred_value_check\", \"path\": \"prompts/q48_reopen_deferred_value_check.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 670, \"queue_reason\": \"Review deferred tasks after Q38-Q47; reopen only if new facts change expected value.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-30T00:14:00Z\", \"handle\": \"1ffe76ca\", \"prompt_hash\": \"b6dc17348fd665f7152d690419ee9397704098de684b05b2cdaeae1ad6b2827b\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-30T00:28:00Z\", \"result\": \"DONE. 11 rows reviewed: 1 re-queued (narrowed), 6 CLOSED, 4 confirmed deferred with re-verified reasons. No submission, quota 0/5. THE ONE RE-OPENING is q28, because its OWN deferral condition ('revisit only if a measurement error recurs') FIRED FOUR TIMES IN ~6 HOURS: Q56's 12-well smoke over-stated its effect by 58% AND PASSED the three-part gate (+0.6050/91.7%/+0.0836) where the 760-well run FAILED it (+0.2541/68.9%/-0.3238); Q57's 8-well smoke supported a conclusion ('the DP declines the freedom it is given') that the 40-well run contradicted (dip active 42-46% of steps, path deviation 4.9 -> 21.1 ft); Q58 found the aligned frame's per-row nnb/closest_surv are NOT the deployed structural-field gate (2139 rows wrong, 6 boundary wells); Q46 found api.kernels_output serves the LATEST version, not the submitted artifact. Re-opened as q28_measurement_traps_ledger at priority 672, deliberately NOT the general audit: one page of pre-flight checks plus the incident table, no CPU, no submission, changes no conclusion, and required to separate traps ALREADY ENFORCED IN CODE from those that are only conventions. THE MOST VALUABLE CLOSURE is q25 (submission ensemble), upgraded from 'no evidence it beats a member' to a MEASURED MECHANISM AGAINST IT: best-of-2 is a call option on variance, an ensemble has LOWER variance by construction, and simulating at Q44's implied per-candidate sd 1.70 (400k draws, matching closed forms) gives E[min(p1,p2)] -0.9541 vs E[min(E,p1)] -0.4750, so replacing one member with an ensemble costs +0.479 ft -- it EXACTLY HALVES the option value -- and the ensemble in both slots costs +0.958 ft. Consistent with Q44's independently measured 0.456 diverse-pair value because it is the same quantity. Harmful BEFORE the third-artifact slot cost is counted. THE CHEAPEST CLOSURE is q24 (frontier run-variance control): its objective was achieved externally FOR FREE by Q45's find (5 kernels resubmitted 14 times unchanged, sd 0.027-0.037), a larger and cleaner measurement than several GPU runs plus quota would have bought. ALSO CLOSED: q23 (Q39 did the stage localisation with NO run from code diffs, and Q45 re-priced the residual stages BELOW the measured 0.03 readability floor -- hedge +0.052 at ~1.7 sd, post-SP45 +0.047 at ~1.6 sd); q32 (merged into q22, which is done); q34 (duplicate of q20, which is done); and q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup, which sat on 'hold' with NO RECORDED REASON while carrying can_submit=true max_submit_cost=1 -- a submission-capable row with no rationale, exactly the risk this review removes -- and is closed on substance too since it proposes an EMISSION improvement that Q17 measured as decoupled from DP quality and Q57 showed is the wrong kind (directional content, not AUC). CONFIRMED DEFERRED, each re-verified rather than assumed: q26 STRENGTHENED (Q45's refresh found 1136 kernels, +42%, still nothing below 6.2, and parsed advertised scores are triage-only); q27 stays deferred with a narrower successor RECORDED BUT NOT QUEUED (Q57 sharpened the constraint to DIRECTIONAL content, so the well-posed question is whether any test-available signal predicts the SIGN of the next TVT move out-of-fold -- not queued because the alignment line cannot become submittable before 2026-08-05 so its expected value for the outcome is ~0); q29 date trigger still unmet (needs >= 2026-08-03), with two notes 