uture round does not misread it: a submission object's total_bytes (~31 MB) is the OUTPUT BUNDLE, not the CSV (~464 KB).\"}\n {\"id\": \"q47_final_selection_ui_checklist\", \"path\": \"prompts/q47_final_selection_ui_checklist.md\", \"status\": \"done\", \"priority\": 660, \"queue_reason\": \"Final selection is separate from submitting and costs no quota; owner needs exact operational checklist.\", \"started_at\": \"2026-07-29T23:59:00Z\", \"handle\": \"3a2fed70\", \"prompt_hash\": \"1c910696ad09e71cae3901a1efad75bc82cb3f9ebd242ef3c8729e9824f64539\", \"finished_at\": \"2026-07-30T00:08:00Z\", \"result\": \"DONE. No submission, no selection made, quota 0/5. MECHANISM PROBED, NOT ASSUMED: the Kaggle API has NO final-selection endpoint (the only selection-shaped symbols are the private _select_models_interactively helper for model uploads, competition_leaderboard_*, and competition_team_submissions(team_id:int)) and ApiSubmission has NO `selected`/`is_final` field (date, description, error_description, file_name, private_score, public_score, ref, status, submitted_by, submitted_by_ref, team_name, total_bytes, url), nor does team_public_submission_fields (['id','dateSubmitted','publicScore']). TWO CONSEQUENCES: the selection can only be made in a browser by the owner, AND its state CANNOT BE VERIFIED PROGRAMMATICALLY -- so no future report may claim 'selection verified' without a screenshot or the owner's word. THE HEADLINE: 54844628 ranks 9th of our 20 submissions by public score, so BOTH plausible auto-selection rules EXCLUDE IT -- 'best public 2' gives 54922806+54968060 and 'most recent 2' gives 55064411+54990075, and both of those pairs are FRONTIER-ONLY with family diversity 0. Kaggle's rules language confirms a Final Submission is 'the Submission selected by the user, OR AUTOMATICALLY SELECTED BY KAGGLE in the event not selected by the user', so an automatic selection WILL happen; the exact criterion is unverified and the checklist is deliberately built so that it 