mpt_chars\": 18719, \"reasoning_effort\": \"high\"}\ndiff --git a/.claude/autopilot/state.json b/.claude/autopilot/state.json\nindex 6c2b3fd..4c05102 100644\n--- a/.claude/autopilot/state.json\n+++ b/.claude/autopilot/state.json\n@@ -3,36 +3,23 @@\n   \"branch\": \"codex/autonomous-queue-2026-07-15\",\n   \"pr\": \"https://github.com/Juktong/Kaggle-competition/pull/3\",\n   \"resume_session_id\": \"6f5484a3-b1d6-46b9-810e-88c221cdf545\",\n-  \"current_handle\": null,\n-  \"current_task_id\": null,\n-  \"last_started_at\": \"2026-07-30T01:29:24Z\",\n-  \"last_finished_at\": \"2026-07-30T01:44:24Z\",\n+  \"current_handle\": \"codex_20260731T124220Z_q28_measurement_traps_ledger\",\n+  \"current_task_id\": \"q28_measurement_traps_ledger\",\n+  \"last_started_at\": \"2026-07-31T12:42:20Z\",\n+  \"last_finished_at\": \"2026-07-31T12:50:00Z\",\n   \"last_result\": {\n-    \"task_id\": \"q48_reopen_deferred_value_check\",\n-    \"outcome\": \"done_1_reopened_6_closed_4_confirmed\",\n+    \"task_id\": \"q28_measurement_traps_ledger\",\n+    \"outcome\": \"done_documentation_ledger_and_preflight\",\n     \"submitted\": false,\n     \"quota_used_today\": 0,\n     \"quota_remaining_today\": 5,\n-    \"headline\": \"Q48 reviewed 11 non-active rows: 1 re-queued, 6 closed, 4 confirmed deferred. q28 was re-opened because its own trigger fired -- four measurement traps in ~6 hours, including a 12-well smoke that PASSED the gate the 760-well run FAILED -- and is narrowed to a bounded traps ledger. The most valuable closure is q25: an ensemble is now harmful rather than unevidenced, because best-of-2 is a call option on variance and an ensemble has lower variance by construction -- simulation at Q44's implied sd gives E[min(p1,p2)] -0.954 vs E[min(E,p1)] -0.475, so an ensemble slot EXACTLY HALVES the option value (+0.479 ft) and using it twice destroys it (+0.958). q24's objective was achieved externally for free by Q45's 14-resubmission noise measurement. Also closed q23 (superseded by Q39 with no run, residual stages below Q45's readability floor), q32/q34 (merged/duplicate), and q17's held row which carried can_submit=true with no recorded reason. Every row now has an explicit reason.\",\n-    \"next_task_id\": \"q28_measurement_traps_ledger\"\n+    \"headline\": \"Q28 wrote reports/measurement_traps_ledger.md from existing evidence only. It keeps the four Q46-Q58 trigger incidents traceable, consolidates the earlier statistical, pipeline, artifact, and operational traps, orders a runnable pre-flight by recorded recurrence, and separates call-site code enforcement from conventions a reader must remember. No conclusion changed and no compute, kernel, submission, or quota was used.\",\n+    \"next_task_id\": \"q49_transition_prior_smoke_from_research\"\n   },\n   \"queue_exhausted\": false,\n   \"pending_kaggle_run\": null,\n   \"pending_submission\": null,\n-  \"pending_local_run\": {\n-    \"runs\": [\n-      {\n-        \"task_id\": \"q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing\",\n-        \"what\": \"row-level forward + ancestral-smoothed PF for 760 wells at NS=64 (the deployed config)\",\n-        \"launched_utc\": \"2026-07-29T23:40:00Z\",\n-        \"rate\": \"14 wells / 3.5 min -> ETA ~3.2 h (~02:50 UTC)\",\n-        \"log\": \"reports/logs/q58_pf_produce_2026-07-30.log\",\n-        \"out\": \"/home/ubuntu/.claude/jobs/rogii_sprint_shared/tmp/q58_pf_smoothed_preds.npz\",\n-        \"collect\": \"run scripts/q58_struct_refit.py (fast, pure arithmetic); it reproduces the deployed line exactly first, then sweeps alpha x W nested against s_54844628 = 8.8626\"\n-      }\n-    ],\n-    \"note\": \"2 cores; do not start another CPU-heavy job or relaunch. The evaluator is cheap and can be re-run freely once the producer output exists.\"\n-  },\n+  \"pending_local_run\": null,\n   \"rules_facts\": {\n     \"merger_deadline\": \"2026-07-29T23:59Z (TODAY)\",\n     \"new_entrant_deadline\": \"2026-07-29T23:59Z (TODAY)\",\n@@ -58,5 +45,5 @@\n   },\n   \"final_pair_note\": \"Q44/Q45: slot 2 is settled at 54844628 on measured grounds (worth ~0.46 ft mean / ~0.94 ft tail as the decorrelated member of a best-of-2, and the only submission we hold whose error is decorrelated from the crowd). Slot 1 is TIED ON MEASUREMENT between 54922806 (teammate, 6.563) and 54968060 (ours, 6.643): the 0.080 gap is 2.7 sd of the measured 0.03 public floor, and its only resolvable component is the GR-sigma term Q36 measured as not transferring. Ownership-first costs at most +0.077 and is strictly better in 8 of 24 modelled cells. Owner's judgement, due 2026-08-04, zero quota.\",\n   \"agent_provider\": \"codex\",\n-  \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-31T12:45:00Z\"\n+  \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-31T12:50:00Z\"\n }\ndiff --git a/reports/measurement_traps_ledger.md b/reports/measurement_traps_ledger.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..703c92f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/reports/measurement_traps_ledger.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+# Measurement-traps ledger\n+\n+Date: 2026-07-31  \n+Task: `q28_measurement_traps_ledger`  \n+Scope: documentation from existing reports only; no new measurement, long CPU run, kernel, or submission.\n+\n+## Pre-flight — ordered by recorded recurrence\n+\n+Frequency counts manifestations, not severity: the bad append expression counts as seven file losses, while\n+one smoke that gave several wrong statistics counts as one incident.\n+\n+1. **Preserve the record and make the process observable (7 truncated reports; 2 buffered launches; PID/self-match recurred).** Append with `scripts.append_section.append` (or read and close before opening for write); launch redirected Python as `python3 -u ... | tee ...`; retain the launch PID and confirm it with `ps -o pid,ppid,etime,cmd -p PID` before signalling it. Do not use `pkill -f`, a waiter whose command contains its own pattern, or a producer piped directly to `head`. Capture producer output first, then shorten it.\n+2. **Do not read a smoke as an effect size or conclusion (5 explicit reversals: N1, Q11, Q21, Q56, Q57).** A smoke proves imports, data, patch activation, alignment, output, and sane ranges only. For an alignment conclusion use at least 40 held-out wells; otherwise use the planned full population. Report per-well median/win rate and the 3-well draw before interpreting pooled RMSE.\n+3. **Use the independent unit that will be scored (3 distinct unit errors).** Split by well, never by row or pair; bootstrap 3 wells, not 760; for a well-level segment use `n_wells`, not rows, and compare its spread with `sigma_well/sqrt(n_wells)`. Run `scripts/eval_three_well_gate.py` for a submission candidate.\n+4. **Reproduce the unmodified deployed quantity before measuring a delta (at least Q21, Q46, Q58).** Join on `(well, ridx)`, assert truth equality and full coverage, recover/check constants from the deployed output, and require the OFF/control path to match exactly or to a declared rounding tolerance. A column name, file label, or API default is not provenance.\n+5. **Prove the treatment is reachable and active (N1, Q54, Q57).** Include an exact degeneracy limit, then report changed rows, binding fraction, selected-state activation, and dose response. Zero movement means “inert/unreachable”, not “no effect”.\n+6. **Score the final objective and accumulated action (Q13, Q17, Q40).** AUC, pointwise argmax error, objective cost, and per-step magnitude are diagnostics only. Run the DP/final pipeline and, for directional path terms, report `abs(estimate) * steps`.\n+7. **Keep selection and attribution out of the scored sample.** Choose hyperparameters on disjoint wells and score on held-out wells; preserve the averaging/shrinkage baseline; change one active factor; never derive a calibration signal and its target from the same truncated run. Treat a public regression as information under Policy Rule 3, not as noise to explain away.\n+\n+## Incident ledger\n+\n+| Trap | Symptom as first seen | Mechanism | Specific check that catches it | Round / source |\n+|---|---|---|---|---|\n+| Q56 smoke size | The 12-well smoke passed all three gates at `+0.6050 / 91.7% / +0.0836`; 760 wells gave `+0.2541 / 68.9% / -0.3238`. | Easier smoke wells (`7.88` forward RMSE vs `9.29`) overstated a real effect by 58%. | Treat smoke as activation only; run the full well population and recompute the three-part gate. | Q56, [PF backward smoothing](q56_pf_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md) |\n+| Q57 smoke conclusion | An 8-well draft said the DP declined added freedom; at 40 wells dip was active on 42–46% of steps and path deviation rose `4.9 -> 21.1` ft. | The illustrative smoke well kept dip nearly off, so it did not exercise the mechanism. | Require activation rates and the predeclared >=40-well result before mechanism prose. | Q57, [dip-state DP](q57_dip_state_augmented_dp_2026-07-30.md) |\n+| Q58 saved column != deployed gate | Using aligned-frame `nnb/closest_surv` left 2,139 rows wrong and RMSE `8.8634` vs `8.8626`, concentrated in six boundary wells. | Deployment used `struct_oof.npz` per-well `meta_nnb/meta_closest`, not the similarly named saved row columns. | Rebuild the unchanged deployed column first; assert coverage by `(well,ridx)` and compare row deltas, gate rate, RMSE, and implied `W`. | Q58, [honest smoother refit](q58_honest_kernel_backward_smoothing_2026-07-30.md) |\n+| Q46 API default != submitted artifact | Three kernels scoring `6.563 / 6.669 / 6.678` returned one byte-identical file. | `api.kernels_output(slug)` serves the latest kernel version, not the submission’s `scriptVersionId`. | Resolve slug + version from the submission URL; verify SHA or a submission-time pairwise delta; use version-history output when versions differ. | Q46, [submission asset inventory](q46_submission_asset_inventory_2026-07-30.md) |\n+| Small-set sweep as validation | N1’s 12-well minimum and Q11/Q21 smokes reversed at 40/773 wells. | Config selection and reporting reused an unrepresentative small sample; pooled tails hid the per-well sign. | Nested selection on disjoint wells, >=40 alignment wells, plus per-well and 3-well statistics. | N1, [geometry-bound DP](n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md); Q11, [PF ranker](q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md) |\n+| Wrong statistical unit (Policy Rule 1; N3; Q42) | A “stable” 760-well bootstrap passed before `54878409` regressed; pair-split AUC chose the wrong window; row-heavy segment spreads vanished across well halves. | Rows/pairs within a well are correlated; their count is not the independent sample size or competition draw. | Split/resample by well; use a 3-well bootstrap; compare segment spread to `sigma_well/sqrt(n_wells)`. | [post-54878409 policy](submission_policy_after_54878409_2026-07-22.md); N3 in [candidate queue](rotation_candidate_queue_2026-07-26.md); Q42, [error taxonomy](q42_honest_line_error_taxonomy_2026-07-30.md) |\n+| Public loss dismissed (Policy Rule 3) | Local OOF improved while public worsened, inviting the loss to be called noise. | Public and private are row splits of the same three wells; transfer is weak for small margins, not irrelevant. | Record the public direction; do not promote a local-only candidate or argue away a public regression. | `54878409`, [post-54878409 policy](submission_policy_after_54878409_2026-07-22.md) |\n+| Selection/oracle mistaken for achievable gain (empirical Rule #1) | Large oracle headroom suggested a path selector; every learned selector lost to the PF aggregate. | Hard selection discards variance reduction; averaging/shrinkage transferred more reliably than fitted choices. | Always score the untouched aggregate and nested-selected arm; require gain over the aggregate, not over a weak single path. | Q11, [PF ranker](q11_twh1_pf_seed_ranker_2026-07-29.md) |\n+| Proxy metric != trajectory target | Q13 improved pointwise emission error by 36.3 ft yet worsened every DP arm; Q17 found AUC and DP RMSE decoupled. | A directional emission bias accumulates along a path; rowwise AUC/argmax cannot see that. | Validate every emission change on DP output, with an exact unchanged-emission reproduction. | Q13, [hybrid emission](q13_twh1_self_hybrid_emission_2026-07-29.md); Q17, [emission exchange rate](q17_kaggle_gpu_tiny_training_followup_2026-07-29.md) |\n+| Per-step term != total effect | A near-zero median drift prior was expected to be neutral but was the worst Q40 family. | A small directional error compounds over a median 477 DP steps; damage tracked `abs(mu)` at correlation `+0.796`. | Report `abs(mu) * steps`, an exact `mu=0` degeneracy control, and final DP RMSE. | Q40, [transition search](q40_transition_model_search_2026-07-30.md) |\n+| Inert/unreachable constraint | N1 first measured 0% binding with the wrong diagnostic; Q54’s `C=40` corridor bound 0%; Q57’s global beam pruned every nonzero dip. | The metric looked after the treatment had already acted, the grid never bit, or search made the arm unreachable. | Exact OFF limit plus direct binding/activation counts before reading outcome. | N1, [geometry-bound DP](n1_geometry_bounded_alignment_2026-07-28.md); Q54, [hard corridor](q54_dp_hard_path_constraints_2026-07-30.md); Q57 above |\n+| Confounded calibration | Same-truncated-run calibration explained 43.4%/14.1%; deployment-honest pairing fell to 3.5%/0.5%. | Signal and target shared the same artificial shorter-prefix degradation. | Construct the signal from the information available at inference and the target from a disjoint/full-prefix run. | G3.5, [rotation status](rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md#round-5--2026-07-28-0550-utc-autopilot-g35_honest_prefix_calibration) |\n+| Destructive “append” | Seven reports lost history and retained only the newest section. | Python evaluates `open(path,'w')` before the inner read, truncating the file. | Use `append_section.append`; compare before/after line count or diff before commit. | 2026-07-28 incident, [rotation status](rotation_pipeline_status_2026-07-26.md#incident--2026-07-28-141x-utc-report-truncation-and-repair) |\n+| Process self-match / wrong PID | `pgrep -f ... | head -1` selected a transient PID; a waiter matched its own command and never exited. | Pattern search sees helper/waiter command lines as well as the target. | Keep the child PID from launch and verify its full command with `ps` before signalling. | Q16, [residual router](q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md) |\n+| Buffered log mistaken for a hang | Two Python launches left a 0-byte log for 20 minutes. | Redirected stdout was block-buffered. | Launch long Python with `-u`/`PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1`, `tee`, and a progress heartbeat. | Q16, [residual router](q16_honest_twh1_residual_router_2026-07-29.md) |\n+| `head` closes a live producer | A producer can emit `BrokenPipeError`/SIGPIPE when `head` exits after N lines; with `pipefail` this can turn a successful query into a failed pre-flight. | The consumer closes the pipe while the producer is still writing. | Capture output (and producer exit code) first; shorten the completed text afterward with a reader that consumes all input. | Named in the Q28 prompt; no earlier project report records a round. It manifested during Q28’s live Kaggle refresh and is first consolidated here. |\n+\n+## Enforcement status\n+\n+**Present in code (at the named call sites, not as a repository-wide framework):** `scripts/eval_three_well_gate.py`\n+implements Policy Rule 1; Q36/Q56/Q58 check `(well,ridx)` alignment and truth equality; Q56 derives its\n+trellis twin through unique anchored insertions and requires `np.array_equal` against the deployed PF, and\n+Q58 reruns that control; Q57 asserts the zero-dip degeneracy; `scripts.append_section.append` reads and\n+closes before writing. These checks fail loudly where those scripts are used.\n+\n+**Convention only — a reader must still remember these:** smoke is activation-only; >=40/full-scale and\n+nested-by-well interpretation; well-level effective sample size; Policy Rule 3’s reading of public loss;\n+preserving the averaging baseline; scoring DP/final output rather than a proxy; accumulated-pull reporting;\n+generic binding/activation checks; deployment-source and submitted-version provenance; one-active-factor\n+attribution; independent calibration signal/target; `python3 -u`; retained/verified PIDs; and avoiding live\n+producer-to-`head` pipelines. The Q58 gate-source check is also not encoded as schema provenance, so a new\n+consumer can still select the wrong columns unless it first reproduces the deployed output.\n+\n+This ledger changes no technical conclusion or slot recommendation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
